 trust to deliver.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to grow, shape the future of fintech and join an ambitious, high-performing team, this is the place for you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Implementation Manager, you'll own the post-sales integration phase for Mollie's largest and most complex deals, guiding merchants from handover through testing to go live. You'll run kickoffs with internal and external stakeholders, set go live dates, keep progress on track, and coordinate testing and feedback along the way. You'll work closely with colleagues across sales, product and engineering, as well as with merchants directly, keeping everyone aligned as deals move toward launch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This function is newly formed, so you'll have real influence over how the role and its processes take shape, bringing in your own experience rather than following a fixed playbook. The role is also more technical than it might first appear: you'll get close to the real world edge cases and issues that surface once a solution meets implementation reality, giving you hands on technical exposure without needing a payments or engineering background going in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work protects revenue by keeping live dates on track, and it supports how Mollie scales delivery more broadly, building a structured, dedicated integration phase for its biggest deals. You'll report to Jan-Jaap van Helden.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll ship</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the post sales integration phase for Mollie's largest and most complex deals, from handover through testing to go live</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run kickoffs with internal and external stakeholders, setting go live dates and keeping progress on track</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organise and track testing, raising issues and feedback as they surface</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate across sales, product and engineering colleagues, as well as with merchants directly, to keep everyone aligned</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep agreed go live dates on track, since delays mean missed revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain documentation and playbooks that make delivery predictable and scalable</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to 3 years of experience in ecommerce or payments, in a similar role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in German and English, since this role supports the German market and works directly with local merchants</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational and structuring skills, with solid project management ability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine technical interest and the ability to understand technical concepts such as APIs, since this role gets close to the edge cases that surface once a solution meets reality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An ownership mindset, taking charge of the implementation process rather than reacting to it, while staying flexible within agreed roles and processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Honest, open communication style with a genuine, trustworthy manner, including a strong track record collaborating with pre-sales teams and handling conflict at handover</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payments or ecommerce experience, or familiarity with the ecosystem, is a strong plus though not required</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow your way</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Mollie, growth is personal. We believe everyone should have the chance to develop their skills, explore new challenges and shape their career on their own terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get regular feedback and performance reviews to support your development, with fair and transparent salary reviews along the way. Many Mollies move into new roles or take on new projects to stretch themselves, and we actively hire from within to help you take the next step.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">No matter if you're aiming for promotion, exploring a different career path or building new skills, you'll be supported with the tools, trust and opportunities to grow your way.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlock your full potential and join us to eliminate financial bureaucracy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by the idea of building what's next, for yourself and for thousands of businesses across Europe, we'd love to hear from you. Apply with your CV (in English) using the form below.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want a peek behind the scenes? Check out what life at Mollie is really like.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Mollie</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in Always Be Shipping, and AI brings that philosophy to life across every team, every role, every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is core to how we build. It helps us move faster, simplify work and make smarter decisions, creating real impact for the businesses we serve. We're looking for people who are excited to use AI to shape the future of finance with us.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mollie/implementation-manager-dach-munich-450423","tags":["Go To Market"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1794606016},{"slug":"prevention-analyst-pentesting-berlin-445105","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Prevention Analyst - Pentesting","description":"<h1><strong>Prevention Analyst - Pentesting</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About this role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We are looking for a Prevention Analyst - Pentester, to join our Prevention track. An attacker does not look at one server in isolation. They look at everything a company exposes to the internet and work out where to start. You will do the same for our clients, taking the attacker’s view of their external attack surface, seeing what an attacker sees, and doing what an attacker would do next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That means reading the story behind an attack surface. A forgotten subdomain, an old login portal, and a misconfigured mail server may each look minor on their own. Together they can show how an organisation has grown, where its blind spots are, and where someone could get in. When you find a potential weak point, you dig into it technically to find out how far an attacker could actually go.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a classic penetration testing role. The deep dive draws on pentest methodology and expertise, but it is not a full pentest, and you will not spend your weeks writing long reports. We focus on finding the high impact vulnerabilities that need attention now and getting them to the client in a form they can act on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is for someone with hands on pentesting experience who wants to work across many customer environments, sharpen their attacker mindset, and grow into owning complex prevention engagements end to end. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess clients’ external attack surface as a whole, from the attacker’s perspective.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify gaps and weaknesses across the surface, not just within a single asset, and work out how they connect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run technical deep dives into potential weak points to establish how far an attacker could get in practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Separate what needs fixing now from what does not, and focus on high and critical findings with immediate impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn technical findings into short, clear advice that clients can understand and act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share what you learn with the team and actively pick up what others know. We work on problems together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to improving our approach, sharing ideas that make assessments faster, clearer, and more useful for clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will need</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands on penetration testing experience and a solid grasp of pentest methodology, particularly for external infrastructure and web applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to think like an attacker, to look at a set of exposed assets and see where you would start and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good judgement about real world impact, so you can tell an interesting finding from an urgent one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to explain technical findings to non technical readers, briefly and without losing accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative way of working and a genuine interest in learning and growing with colleagues, not working as a solo player.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working across multiple client environments in parallel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Certifications such as OSCP, BSCP, or CPTS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven bug bounty track record or other real world offensive security experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with SMEs or mid market customers on security topics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A meaningful mission, protecting organisations across Europe from real world cyber threats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with top tier professionals from national CERTs, intelligence agencies, and leading tech backgrounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A remote friendly culture with quarterly meetups and annual company retreats, for example in Spain, Portugal, or Italy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thursday socials to stay connected.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A generous time off policy, including wellbeing and volunteering days.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Eye Security</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Eye Security is providing cybersecurity with embedded cyber insurance solutions for organisations across Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we are already over 190 FTEs and continue to grow internationally, having secured our Series C funding of 60 million.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We combine cutting edge technology with hands on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team brings together talent from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds, all united by a shared mission, to make enterprise grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Eye, you will work on projects with an international footprint, solving real world challenges and helping to build a safer digital future for our clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to making our hiring process accessible to everyone. If you need a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview for this role, please inform the TA team.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/eye-security/prevention-analyst-pentesting-berlin-445105","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin - hybrid","created_at":1794606016},{"slug":"senior-msp-partner-manager-germany-berlin-355149","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"(Senior) MSP Partner Manager Germany (m/f/x)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an MSP Partner Manager, you will be responsible for building our partnership and sales network with security-oriented partnerships to sell with and through Managed Service Providers (MSPs). Throughout the process, the focus will be on building and maintaining relationships with our customers, using your network to engage with potential partners and customers. You will report directly to the CRO and work closely with our sales and marketing team to jointly identify and capitalize on opportunities.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and expand Eye’s MSP partner ecosystem within an assigned region in Germany.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and onboard new partners, developing long-term relationships based on trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support partners from initial discussions through contracts, onboarding, and business planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with partners on joint go-to-market initiatives and ensure mutual growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Eye at partner meetings, trade fairs, and industry events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with colleagues across Sales, Marketing, and other teams to align efforts and maximize impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will need:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years of professional experience as MSP Partner Manager or Channel Sales Manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in building and expanding partnerships, either by working directly with managed service providers (MSPs), developing a partner ecosystem or driving new business in a SaaS or software environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong commercial acumen and a proactive, hunter-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in software or SaaS sales, cybersecurity knowledge is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent relationship-building and communication skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in German, with good command of English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexibility and willingness to travel regularly within your assigned region</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will become part of one of the fastest growing cybersecurity scale-ups in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will play a key role in building an innovative cybersecurity product line where we combine effective cybersecurity with cyber insurance on a global scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will evolve alongside the industry - as a rapidly growing scale-up, we provide an environment where your professional development is driven by the dynamic nature of our work and the complexity of the problems we solve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will enjoy a flexible work setup that supports our distributed team in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An attractive remuneration package and bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Car allowance and “floating holidays” for additional time off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MacBook or Windows Laptop and iPhone or Samsung company phone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong support for your personal and professional development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular company-wide get-togethers, giving you the opportunity to collaborate in person and build strong team connections.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Eye</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security is providing cybersecurity with embedded cyber insurance solutions for organizations in Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we are already over 180 FTEs and continue to grow internationally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We combine cutting-edge technology with hands-on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team brings together talent from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds, all united by a shared mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Eye, you will work on projects with an international footprint, solving real-world challenges and helping to build a safer digital future for our clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/eye-security/senior-msp-partner-manager-germany-berlin-355149","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1794606016},{"slug":"remote-solution-consulting-manager-286794","company_name":"Rillet","title":"Solution Consulting Manager","description":"<h1>What We Do</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet serves accounting and finance teams, the financial brains of their companies. Our job is to help them run the numbers with impossible speed, accuracy, and insight.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet is the Agentic ERP built for modern finance teams. We help companies automate the most critical parts of finance, from closing the books and recognizing revenue to consolidating entities and reporting to investors. More than 600 companies run on Rillet, including Mercor, Scribe, and Function Health, and we partner with leading accounting firms including EY and KPMG.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building in one of the largest software markets in the world, with the momentum to match. Rillet has raised more than $200M, is valued at $1B, and is backed by Sequoia, a16z, ICONIQ, Bain Capital Ventures, Oak HC/FT, and other leading investors. We’re using that backing to build the financial infrastructure for the next generation of companies and help every business run its numbers at the speed of AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who We Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet’s pace is not for everyone. Intelligence is table stakes. To succeed here, you need extreme speed, agency, and flexibility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The people who thrive at Rillet do not wait for assignments. They internalize the mission, design a strategy, and bring back results that are better, faster, and more creative than a manager could have asked for.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work revolves around our customers. The people who succeed here are energized by delivering what matters most, even when it was not part of the original plan.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rillet is built on deep accounting expertise, and it takes people from many disciplines to build a category-defining company. You do not need to be an accountant to thrive here. You do need to care deeply about the problems we solve and the impact our customers can create. Together, we combine the precision of accounting with the speed, creativity, and ambition of AI-native software to power the financial core of the world’s fastest-growing companies while redefining what finance teams should expect from their software.</p><h2><strong>The Role</strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have grown quickly, and our Solution Consulting team is at the center of how prospects evaluate Rillet as their next ERP. We are looking for a Solution Consulting Manager to lead and scale that team.<br /><br />This is a player-coach role weighted heavily toward coaching. You will spend roughly <strong>25% of your time running your own sales cycles </strong>(staying sharp, credible and close to the customer and product) and roughly <strong>75% of your time coaching, mentoring and developing your team</strong>, primarily by riding shotgun on live deals and giving real-time feedback. You will also be a key voice in shaping the product and building the Solution Consulting infrastructure that lets the organization scale.<br /><br />You will work directly with the CEO, GTM leadership and the Product team.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong><br /></h2><h2><strong>Coach, mentor and develop the team (~75%)</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ride shotgun on deals. </strong>Join discovery calls, demos, technical validations and POCs to observe, step in when needed, and give specific, real-time feedback. Run tight pre-call prep and post-call debriefs so every deal is a learning opportunity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Raise the bar on craft. </strong>Coach Solution Consultants on discovery, value selling, storytelling, demo design, handling technical objections, and tailoring sandbox environments to each customer's use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow each person individually. </strong>Set clear expectations and development plans, give regular honest feedback, and help each Solution Consultant build deep product and accounting domain expertise and advance in their career.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hire and onboard. </strong>Recruit, interview and ramp new Solution Consultants, and build an onboarding program that gets them deal-ready quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner on deal strategy. </strong>Work with Account Executives and sales leadership to staff deals, pressure-test strategy on complex ERP evaluations, and keep technical wins on track.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Run your own sales cycles (~25%)</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remove technical objections. </strong>Take on strategic and complex opportunities, understanding the prospect's business requirements and existing technology stack, and clearly articulating how Rillet integrates and improves their processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deliver high-impact demos. </strong>Set up and tailor the sandbox environment, answer questions in real time, and act as the prospect's trusted consultant throughout the purchase process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Represent Rillet. </strong>Be the face of the company, applying high customer empathy and structured problem-solving to ensure every prospect interaction is excellent, including with finance and accounting leaders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Inform product and build for scale</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the voice of the prospect. </strong>Synthesize front-line feedback, objections, competitive intel and feature gaps from across the team, and bring it to founders and Product in close to real time, with clear patterns and prioritization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Influence the roadmap. </strong>Partner with Product on discovery, early feedback on new features, and how capabilities are positioned and demoed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build Solution Consulting infrastructure. </strong>Create the systems, playbooks and tools that help the team scale, such as discovery frameworks, demo standards and reusable assets, sandbox and demo-data templates, technical FAQs and objection libraries, POC and technical-validation processes, a deal-review cadence, and enablement and certification paths.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure what matters. </strong>Define and track team metrics (technical win rate, ramp time, deal coverage, cycle time) and use them to improve how the team operates.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years managing or formally mentoring pre-sales, solutions consulting or sales engineering teams, with a track record of developing people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of industry accounting experience across areas such as revenue recognition, month-end close and multi-entity consolidation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years supporting complex ERP sales cycles with implementation and/or customer support for accounting or financial solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of the ecosystem of tools in the office of the CFO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communicator who makes complex concepts easy to understand, and who can give direct, constructive feedback in the moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building processes, enablement or tooling for a growing team, ideally in an early-stage, fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thrives in a dynamic environment while keeping high attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CPA certification or having started your career in audit is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Note</strong>: All official Rillet recruiting communications will come from an @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://rillet.com">rillet.com</a> email address. If you’re contacted from another domain, please disregard the message and report it as spam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Life at Rillet</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow with us.</strong> Take meaningful ownership, expand your scope, and make an impact as Rillet scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive pay and meaningful equity.</strong> Be rewarded for the value you help create.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits that support you.</strong> We offer competitive benefits designed to support your health, wellbeing, time away from work, family, and long-term financial goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Better together.</strong> We value collaboration, connection, and spending meaningful time together as a team. We regularly create opportunities to connect through team meals, events, and company gatherings.</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: $210K – $320K • Offers Equity • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>Zone A • OTE $225K – $320K • Offers Equity</li><li>Zone B • OTE $210K – $290K • Offers Equity</li><li>Zone C • OTE $210K – $290K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/rillet/remote-solution-consulting-manager-286794","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1794606016},{"slug":"software-development-engineer-in-test-ii-navnative-mapbox-germany-325475","company_name":"Mapbox","title":"Software Development Engineer in Test II, NavNative","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Mapbox is the leading real-time location platform for a new generation of location-aware businesses. Mapbox is the only platform that equips organizations with the full set of tools to power the navigation of people, packages, and vehicles everywhere. More than 4 million registered developers have chosen Mapbox because of the platform’s flexibility, security and privacy compliance. Organizations use Mapbox applications, data, SDKs and APIs to create customized and immersive experiences that delight their customers. </p><h2><strong>What We Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Navigation Native team builds the high-performance C++ engine that serves as the "brain" of our Navigation SDKs. This library runs directly on end-user systems (on-board), powering everything from mobile apps to in-vehicle infotainment systems for partners like BMW, Porsche, and Zeekr.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We solve the fundamental challenges of movement: transforming noisy GPS/IMU data into precise map-matching, managing complex road-network graphs, supporting routes and alternatives, tracking progress along a route, and providing "Electronic Horizon" capabilities for ADAS. Our work happens at the edge, supporting location frequencies up to 10Hz and ensuring a seamless experience even in tunnels or dense urban canyons.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As AI becomes embedded in modern engineering workflows, we value engineers who can thoughtfully integrate AI into design, development, and decision-making. Our interview process will include discussion of how you use AI in your engineering workflow.<br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for smart, fast-learning engineers who care as much about proving that navigation works as about making it work. As an SDE(T), you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the unit, integration, and functional test architecture for a C++17 library, and the CMake and CI pipelines that run it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn real-world location recordings into regression tests, and define the quality metrics for map-matching, routing, and route-following.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the quality signal fast and trustworthy: eliminate flaky tests, run sanitizer and performance builds, and track coverage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI-driven test tooling: agent-based test generation, automated dogfooding and triage, and AI-assisted PR review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with feature engineers on testability and review designs for how they will be verified.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thoughtfully leverage AI tools in your workflow and set the standard for how the team uses them. </p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Believe Are Important Traits for This Role</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> 5+ years of experience in C++17: comfortable writing test code and tooling, reading production code, and debugging with sanitizers and profilers. Python or similar for harnesses and analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building test infrastructure for a large native codebase: test frameworks, CMake, and CI systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A data-driven mindset: you define metrics, build the tooling to measure them, and use them to argue for or against a change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience diagnosing hard-to-reproduce failures: flakiness, platform-specific behavior, memory and threading bugs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong English skills, with the ability to explain test results, risk, and trade-offs to peers and stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Would be a Plus</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with navigation concepts (map matching, dead reckoning, route progress, or Electronic Horizon).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with replay- or simulation-based testing using real sensor and GPS data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building AI- or agent-based developer tooling for testing, code review, or triage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with coverage tooling, performance benchmarking, or testing SDKs through generated bindings.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Employment Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employment Type:</strong> Full-time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Weekly Hours:</strong> 40 h per week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location/Hybrid Policy:</strong> Remote (from any city in Germany)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Value</h2></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.mapbox.com/about/values/">our core values</a>, which are not unique to this position and are necessary for Mapbox leaders:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value high-performing creative individuals who dig into problems and opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in individuals being their whole selves at work. We commit to this through supportive health care, parental leave, flexibility for the things that come up in life, and innovating on how we think about supporting our people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We emphasize an environment of teaching and learning to equip employees with the tools needed to be successful in their function and the company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We strongly believe in the value of growing a diverse team and encourage people of all backgrounds, genders, ethnicities, abilities, and sexual orientations to apply.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How We Support You</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid/Remote Options: </strong>Enjoy flexibility to work comfortably from home or periodically from an office where applicable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Country-Specific Care &amp; Coverage: </strong>Private health, dental, and income protection plans tailored to elevate your regional statutory benefits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family-First Support:</strong> Family care, maternity and paternity leave policies to support your growing family.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lifestyle Spending Account: </strong>Contributions to support your health, wellness, and personal growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Balance &amp; Brainpower: </strong>Mental health support for you and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rest &amp; Recharge:</strong> Paid time away, company holidays, and generous absence policies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time Off to Give Back: </strong>Dedicated paid volunteering time in addition to your standard PTO.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By applying for this position, you acknowledge that you have received the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.mapbox.com/legal/applicant-privacy-notice/">Mapbox Non-US Privacy Notice</a> for applicants, which is linked here.  Completing this application requires you to provide personal data, such as your name and contact information, which is mandatory for Mapbox to process your application. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We are committed to a fair and equitable hiring process. We do not discriminate against any protected class.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />#LI-Remote</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mapbox/software-development-engineer-in-test-ii-navnative-mapbox-germany-325475","tags":["Navigation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Mapbox Germany","created_at":1794606015},{"slug":"staff-robotics-engineer-physical-ai-berlin-285099","company_name":"Almetra","title":"Staff Robotics Engineer – Physical AI (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in reshaping manufacturing with advanced tech like computer vision and AI! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Staff Robotics Engineer – Physical AI (m/f/d)</strong>, you will be integral in driving our company's next phase of innovation - automating industrial processes to address the scarcity of skilled labor. We have already proven our ability to optimize processes and increase efficiency, and now we are determined to automate tasks within industrial environments. Your main focus will be on R&amp;D and will involve building and showcasing a demonstrator that utilizes industrial robot arms to automate currently manual tasks. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong background in state of the art in robotic manipulation, extensive experience in modeling, planning, and controlling robotic systems, as well as applying machine learning techniques to enhance robotic manipulation capabilities.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead R&amp;D efforts to prototype a new roboti