tion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a founding voice in shaping Dandy’s German sales motion, messaging, and processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consistently track activity, pipeline, and performance in Salesforce</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Become a student of dentistry and an expert in Dandy’s product and value proposition</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with senior sales leadership to hit revenue targets and refine KPIs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operate with urgency, accountability, and a bias toward action in a fast-moving environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of sales experience, with 3+ year owning a full-cycle closing role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Language requirements: Fluent English and native-level German</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a high-growth startup or scaling environment strongly preferred</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating in ambiguity with limited structure and resources</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational skills and disciplined pipeline management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High proficiency with Salesforce or similar CRMs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated track record of professional success</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Req ID:</strong> J-1199</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For full-time positions, Dandy offers a wide range of best-in-class, comprehensive, and inclusive benefits tailored to each country where we operate. Our local benefits packages typically include healthcare, dental, mental health support, parental planning resources, retirement savings options, and generous paid time off—ensuring our team members are supported no matter where they live and work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dandy is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive culture that celebrates authenticity to win as one. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, protected veteran status, citizenship or immigration status, or any other legally protected characteristics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dandy also fully complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). We are dedicated to embracing challenges and creating an accessible, inclusive workplace for all individuals. If you require any accommodations for your interview or have any questions beforehand, rest assured that we will do everything we can to meet your needs. Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.meetdandy.com/careers/">Dandy Careers</a> for more! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data Privacy Notice: By submitting your application, you consent to Dandy collecting, storing, and processing your personal information for recruitment purposes in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.meetdandy.com/privacy-policy/"><u>Privacy Policy</u></a> and GDPR regulations. You have the right to access, rectify, or request the deletion of your data at any time by contacting <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.meetdandy.com/privacy-requests/"><u>Privacy Requests</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/dandy/smb-account-executive-berlin-309181","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany - Berlin","created_at":1794595219},{"slug":"senior-talent-acquisition-partner-berlin-7139","company_name":"Parloa","title":"Senior Talent Acquisition Partner","description":"<h2>About Parloa</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Parloa's mission is to make every customer conversation feel effortless for both customers and the companies serving them. As agentic AI accelerates, Parloans are shaping the foundation of a new era in customer experience, one where customer support is no longer transactions, but meaningful exchanges. It is not just a vision; Parloa has powered over ONE BILLION interactions between global enterprise brands and their customers, with companies like Booking.com,  HealthEquity, Allianz, SAP, BarmeniaGothaer, and TUI already deploying Parloa at scale.</p><h2><strong>About the role:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Senior Talent Acquisition Partner</strong> at Parloa, you'll own hiring for the engineers building the core of our agentic AI platform. You'll act as a strategic partner to Engineering leadership and lead complex, senior, and business-critical searches across Backend, Platform, Infrastructure, AI/ML, and Product Engineering. You'll help us grow our engineering organization with speed, rigor, and a candidate experience that reflects the quality of the product we build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is for someone who speaks engineers' language, earns the trust of technical leaders, and independently drives hiring outcomes in one of Europe's most competitive talent markets. You won't just fill roles. You'll help shape how we attract, assess, and close the engineers defining the future of AI-driven customer experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Areas of ownership:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own full-cycle recruiting</strong> for Software Engineering roles from Senior to Staff/Principal level, including hard-to-fill AI/ML and infrastructure searches</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner closely with Engineering Managers, Directors, and VPs</strong> to define profiles, calibrate levels, and align on market realities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and maintain high-quality pipelines</strong> through proactive sourcing, market mapping, and targeted outreach across Europe</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Advise on leveling and compensation positioning</strong>, helping hiring teams make confident, well-calibrated decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deliver against key recruiting metrics</strong>, including time-to-fill, pipeline conversion, offer acceptance rate, and quality of hire</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run structured, fair technical hiring processes</strong> in partnership with interviewers and bar raisers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Create a thoughtful, engaging candidate experience</strong> from first touch through close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage relocation and visa-related hiring conversations</strong> alongside our People team for international candidates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Share talent intelligence</strong> on competitor landscapes, compensation trends, and hiring hotspots to influence strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a senior member of the Talent team by <strong>raising the bar on execution</strong> and technical hiring quality</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Someone who has extensive experience in the software engineering recruitment industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven experience closing senior and Staff-level engineers</strong> in a startup, scale-up, or high-growth SaaS environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong technical fluency</strong>: you understand engineering disciplines, tech stacks, and levels well enough to hold credible conversations with candidates and hiring managers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellent sourcing ability</strong>, with a track record of building pipelines in competitive European markets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience <strong>leveraging AI tools</strong> and recruiting technology to improve sourcing, engagement, and efficiency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong stakeholder management skills</strong>, with the confidence to advise, challenge, and influence engineering leaders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-driven approach</strong>, using funnel metrics and market data to improve outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with <strong>Greenhouse and/or Ashby</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience hiring <strong>internationally, including relocation and visa processes</strong>, is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent English</strong>; German is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our recruiting process:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talent Acquisition → Hiring Manager → Technical Interview(s) → Bar Raiser</p><h2>Why Parloa?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're at the beginning of a new era in customer experience, one where AI doesn't just respond, but understands, reasons, and takes action. We're building agentic AI that enterprises trust with their most important customer moments: complex questions, high volumes, real stakes. When millions of people reach out to a brand, those interactions aren't just support tickets; they're defining experiences. We're here to raise the standard: making every conversation seamless, intelligent, and genuinely helpful. If you care about shaping how businesses and customers connect at scale and want your work to matter in real, everyday moments, this is where you do it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Parloa, ownership isn't a buzzword; it means being accountable for outcomes, not just tasks. We operate in a c