any_name":"Tonies","title":"Team Lead Functional Analyst (all genders)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">tonies is the world’s leading interactive audio platform for children, with over 12 million Tonieboxes and 173 million Tonies sold globally. Our intuitive, screen-free system empowers children to learn and play independently in a safe and engaging way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With a presence in over 100 countries and a diverse portfolio of ~1,500 Tonies across multiple languages, we continue to redefine how children experience storytelling and learning. Since our IPO in 2021, our global team of 630+ colleagues is united by a shared mission: shaping the future of play, learning, and imagination.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Lead Functional Analyst (all genders)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role &amp; Impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are seeking a strategic, people-focused Team Lead Functional Analyst to head our <strong>Functional Analysis &amp; Process Design</strong> chapter within the Enterprise Applications &amp; Integrations department. As tonies undergoes a company-wide transformation from a distributed landscape to a harmonized, global operating model powered by SAP S/4HANA Public Cloud, our IT and business functions are moving toward a product-oriented organization.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this pivotal role, you will provide horizontal leadership to our team of Functional Analysts -the vital translation bridge between our business value streams (Operations, Finance, Sales) and our technical delivery teams. The ideal candidate combines a deep understanding of <strong><u>end-to-end business processes with a strong mentoring mindset</u></strong>, setting <strong>methodology standards</strong> and <strong>empowering the team to translate operational needs into scalable, standard-first enterprise solutions.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Team Lead Functional Analyst, you will act as the <strong>Chapter Lead</strong> for Functional Analysis, providing both disciplinary leadership and methodological governance for your team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your responsibilities include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Leadership &amp; Development:</strong> Providing horizontal leadership to the Functional Analyst team, overseeing personal skill development, coaching, and managing capacity allocation across various value streams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Methodology &amp; Standards:</strong> Setting and enforcing best-practice methodology standards for the chapter, including process modeling (BPMN 2.0), agile requirements engineering, user story writing (Jira/Confluence), and User Acceptance Testing (UAT) protocols.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Governance:</strong> Empowering your team to act as "The Bridge" that effectively translates business pain points into structured functional specification documents (FSDs) while strictly enforcing Fit-to-Standard and Clean Core principles to prevent unnecessary custom complexity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Partnering seamlessly with Business Product Owners (who prioritize the "WHAT &amp; WHY"), SAP Consultants (The Solution), Solution Architects (The Gatekeepers), and App Engineers (The Build) to ensure a unified end-to-end delivery lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Integrity:</strong> Ensuring your team upholds strict Segregation of Duties (SoD) guidelines and four-pillar controls during process design (e.g., keeping functional analysis strictly separated from system configuration, master data creation, and security mapping).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transformation Stewardship:</strong> Driving the organizational shift from reactive project delivery toward proactive product ownership, helping the business eliminate shadow processes and friction points across boundaries like Order-to-Cash, Procure-to-Pay, and Record-to-Report.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine a deep understanding of process modeling and enterprise platforms with a consultative leadership mindset, and you enjoy empowering teams in complex transformation initiatives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years of <strong>experience in functional analysis, business process design, or requirements engineering within modern enterprise suites</strong> (e.g., SAP S/4HANA Cloud, Salesforce, Microsoft Business Central).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in a <strong>leadership or chapter lead role</strong>, with a strong passion for mentoring, team development, and resource management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep <strong>methodological expertise in BPMN 2.0, Design Thinking, process decomposition</strong>, and defining end-to-end test scenarios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Advanced tooling proficiency </strong>in Jira, Confluence, Signavio/Lucidchart/Miro, and UAT management platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid <strong>understanding of core business domains </strong>such as accounting, supply chain, procurement, or digital retail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional <strong>diplomatic and analytical facilitation skills</strong>; the confidence to constructively challenge business requests and guide stakeholders toward standard solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured, independent, and <strong>solution-oriented way of working</strong> with a clear understanding of cross-system architecture boundaries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; German is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global Teamwork</strong>: We collaborate across departmental and country borders. You’ll be part of a truly international community where every voice is heard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Come as you are:</strong> This applies to the dress code and everything else. We believe you give your best when you feel truly comfortable being yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive Package</strong>: We offer a competitive salary and a range of comprehensive benefits tailored to your specific location, which we’ll share during the recruiting process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration &amp; Community:</strong> We’re big on "we." You’ll join a team that values connection and celebrates wins together, no matter the time zone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Continuous Learning:</strong> Benefit from internal/external training and an individual learning budget to keep your skills as sharp as a Tonie’s ears.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tonie Discounts: </strong>Enjoy attractive discounts on our entire range of products. You’ll quickly become the favorite guest at every birthday party!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rest &amp; Recharge:</strong> Great work requires a clear head. You’ll enjoy generous paid time off to ensure you have plenty of time for your own stories.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>As part of our principles, we are committed to supporting inclusion and diversity at tonies. We actively celebrate our colleagues’ different abilities, ethnicities, faith and gender. Everyone is welcome and supported in their development at all stages in their journey with us. <br /><br />We look forward to hearing from you!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/tonies/team-lead-functional-analyst-all-genders-dusseldorf-116292","tags":["CIO"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Düsseldorf","created_at":1794595218},{"slug":"social-media-manager-working-student-ai-music-video-platform-berlin-302221","company_name":"Neural Frames GmbH","title":"Social Media Manager (Working Student) // AI Music Video Platform","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Neural Frames is a leading AI music video generator, turning any song into a fully produced music video in minutes. We’re bootstrapped, profitable, and generating more than $7M in annualized revenue. Our ambition is to build a category-defining company that helps tens of millions of audio creators visualize and promote their work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our product makes video and our users make thousands of them, so we’re never short of material. Our own social channels don’t show it yet. They’re shared between a few people on top of their other work, and we think they could be much better with one person who owns them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our working student for social media, you’ll own our social channels day to day: posting on TikTok, Instagram and YouTube Shorts, writing captions in our voice, bringing ideas for what we post next, and replying to our users in the comments and on Discord and Reddit. You’ll work closely with the founder and with our marketing team across content, creators, design and paid.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within weeks you’ll see whether your ideas show up in the numbers, and you’ll learn how content turns into signups and revenue at a fast-growing startup.<br /></p><h2>Tasks</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently enrolled at a university in Germany, and able to work around 20 hours per week during the semester</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You spend a lot of time on TikTok and Instagram and know what's going on there: you notice trends early and can tell why one video gets 400 views and another gets 4 million</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write well in English: short, clear and funny when it fits, and you pick up a brand voice quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're full of ideas: show you our product and a few user videos, and you'll have ten things we could post</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've run a social account before, your own or one for a club, band or small brand, and can show it to us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can do basic video edits in CapCut or similar. You don't need to be a video editor</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reliable: your hours are flexible and you plan them around university, but you check in on our channels once a day and keep a steady posting schedule</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You like talking to people online, and you're friendly and patient when someone needs help</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI tools are a normal part of how you work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're into music, AI and internet culture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're based in Berlin and can join us in the office at least one day per week</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently enrolled at a university in Germany, and able to work around 15-20 hours per week during the semester</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You already make content: you've run your own account or one for a club, band or small brand, and can show what you made</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong instincts for short-form content: you can tell why one video gets 400 views and another gets 4 million</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can make the content yourself: script, edit, caption and post (CapCut, Premiere or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reliable and organized: you can plan your hours around university and keep a steady posting schedule</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about numbers: you want to know which posts lead to signups, not just likes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is part of how you work: you use AI tools to ideate, edit and repurpose faster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuinely into music, AI and internet culture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're based in Berlin and can join us in the office at least two days per week</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus points:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've grown your own or a club's account to a real audience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You study marketing, media, communications, film or music</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You make music, or you're close to the music scene</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable on camera</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You edit video well, beyond the basics</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we measure success</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our channels post on a steady schedule, sound like us, and pick up on what's happening while it still matters. Users who comment or ask for help get a friendly, useful answer within a day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over time, we want channels musicians follow, share and talk about, and that make them want to try Neural Frames themselves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Benefits</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible hours around your studies, bi-weekly team lunches, regular team events, an annual summer offsite, learning &amp; development support, productivity tools, and a real path into a full-time growth role after graduating.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Neural Frames is dedicated to creating an equitable, inclusive, and supportive work environment that brings people together from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Our strength is in our differences. We're proud to be an equal opportunity employer and welcome all applicants as we're committed to promoting a culture of opportunity for all.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/neural-frames-gmbh/social-media-manager-working-student-ai-music-video-platform-berlin-302221","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1794595218},{"slug":"business-development-representative-german-speaking-berlin-61617","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Business Development Representative, German speaking","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Mission:</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a proactive business builder who wants to become an expert in the global payments landscape. In this role, you aren't just a "lead generator" - you are a strategic partner to Sales. You will use a blend of highly relevant, strategic outreach, AI-driven insights, and deep technical research to open doors at the world’s most prestigious brands. We expect you to master the complexities of the payments industry to source and support high-intent opportunities that drive actual revenue..</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master the Payments Craft: Rapidly develop a deep, technical understanding of our product suite and global payment trends to act as a consultant to prospective merchants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategic Account Mapping: Conduct in-depth research into organizational structures and competitive landscapes to identify and engage high-value strategic accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced Discovery: Conduct high-level discovery calls that move past the "pitch" to uncover deep technical and business challenges for the merchant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive Growth Momentum: Maintain a high-performing operating rhythm in daily outreach, consistently striving for excellence while contributing to a high-standard team environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the Sales Lifecycle: Partner closely with Sales to move deals through the funnel, providing support on follow-ups and maintaining momentum to ensure successful financial go-lives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-Functional Leadership: Partner with Solutions Engineering, Underwriting, and Product teams to align internal stakeholders and accelerate the sales cycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage AI &amp; Sales Tech: Proactively use AI-driven systems (e.g., Salesforce, intent-data tools) and advanced analytics to optimize lead generation, territory planning, and pipeline accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational Rigor: Maintain a data-backed approach to your territory, utilizing qualification frameworks (like MEDDIC) and keeping the CRM (Salesforce) as a source of truth.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German or Polish Native is essential </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactive Ownership: You take end-to-end accountability for your territory and outcomes, proactively plan your quarter to overachieve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intellectual Curiosity: A relentless drive to learn the mechanics of complex financial technology and industry dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional Communication &amp; Presence: Excellent listening and communication skills (written, verbal, and in person). You have the confidence and clarity to engage effectively with stakeholders at all levels - from internal product leads to C-suite executives at global brands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical &amp; AI Fluency: A desire to leverage the latest sales technology and AI tools to work smarter, not just harder.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional Resilience: A fundamentally positive approach that maintains momentum through setbacks and challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coachability: A track record of actively seeking feedback and immediately implementing it to improve your performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Persistence &amp; Precision: A high level of attention to detail combined with a steadfast commitment to excellence in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team Impact &amp; Collective Success: You believe in winning as a team and contribute to a supportive, inclusive environment where everyone can perform at their best. You are a positive cultural force who shares feedback respectfully and collaborates cross-functionally to help the entire organization improve.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style