oking for ways to unblock delivery and get great ideas to our customers faster, with the support of AI.</span></p><p><br><span style="color:#5a5f72">You are a catalyst: you are there where you are needed most. Sometimes that means being deep in the daily work, supporting the team and even coding along. Sometimes it means making a decision because the team is stuck. And sometimes it means zooming out to improve flows across the whole department. You set direction and pace, and make sure that what we ship reaches customers and moves our quarterly OKRs. You also make room for the bigger picture: business topics, our leveling matrix, and driving AI adoption across engineering together with fellow Engineering Managers.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#5A5F72">Ready to become part of the most important mission on this planet? We are rebuy, pioneers in the sustainable reuse of electronics and media, and we are looking for you! Our mission: to make circular living accessible to all, one transaction at a time. By giving products a second chance, we reduce resource consumption and avoid unnecessary e-waste.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Our team of 500 comes from all corners of the world; we drive things forward collaboratively, take personal responsibility, value positive critical thinking, and persistently serve our customers and planet. </span><br></p><h3><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Lead two customer-facing teams as a catalyst: zoom in to support the daily work and unblock the team when it’s stuck, zoom out to improve flows across the department</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Set direction: make sure the teams understand the “why” behind their topics, own them and are motivated to drive them. Make the call when full consensus isn’t possible, and focus everyone on what is truly urgent</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Own delivery: keep the teams focused on their promise dates, get them to the finish line and course-correct fast. Use modern metrics to track progress and speed</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Stay close to the tech: pair with engineers, review work, join technical discussions, and challenge estimates and trade-offs</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Drive AI adoption across engineering with fellow Engineering Managers (tools, workflows, review standards and measuring real impact), starting in your own teams</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Drive hiring and take care of your people and their growth through regular 1:1s, honest feedback and by evolving our engineering leveling matrix</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Connect product, design and engineering, keep stakeholders informed early, and work with engineering leadership on cross-team strategy</span></p></li></ul> <br> <h3><strong>Requirements:</strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Substantial experience as an Engineering Manager, with a track record of delivering business outcomes. You’re accountable for results, not only team happiness, and comfortable owning and reporting engineering metrics</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">A software engineering background with a strong foothold in at least one of our stacks: Angular/TypeScript, PHP/Symfony or Kotlin/Spring. You don’t need all three, but you can challenge solutions and form an objective view of your teams’ work, even if you don’t code day to day</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">Experience driving or shaping AI adoption in engineering teams, or a strong focus on it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">High self-organization and drive: you spot what’s urgent among many important topics and act on it without waiting to be told</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#5a5f72">The ability to flex between hands-on support, deci