n. Our work connects sensor measurements, machine and robot states, quality data, alarms and expert knowledge. These problems require understanding both the data and its context: a fault may originate elsewhere in a production line, and similar symptoms can have different causes. We are a small, early-stage startup where individual contributions directly shape the product. We value curiosity, initiative and people who enjoy understanding difficult problems and making things work.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>The Role</strong></p><p>We are looking for an experienced, hands-on Software Engineer with strong Python skills and sound technical judgment. You will own backend features from problem definition through implementation, testing, deployment and maintenance.</p><p>After onboarding, you should be able to investigate unfamiliar production code and independently review Python/backend pull requests: understand intended behavior, question assumptions, assess tests and failure paths, and identify effects on the wider system.</p><p>We actively encourage AI-assisted development. You remain responsible for understanding, verifying and maintaining the resulting software. We value demonstrated delivery, ownership and learning ability more than a fixed number of years in the industry.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><ul><li><p>Build backend services, APIs and SQL-backed data pipelines for industrial analytics, knowledge retrieval and agent workflows.</p></li><li><p>Read and improve existing code, review pull requests, and make informed decisions about interfaces, data models, state and failure handling.</p></li><li><p>Design meaningful unit, integration and end-to-end tests, supported by continuous integration.</p></li><li><p>Test with representative machine data, recorded streams and simulated device inputs, including missing measurements, duplicate or out-of-order events, invalid values and connection failures.</p></li><li><p>Reproduce bugs, inspect whether test assertions verify the intended behavior, and add useful regression coverage.</p></li><li><p>Understand manufacturing users and equipment, contribute across integration and deployment, and communicate trade-offs and blockers early.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul><li><p>Strong practical Python and backend engineering skills, supported by software you personally shipped and maintained.</p></li><li><p>Independent code-review ability: you can investigate a change, assess correctness, maintainability and security, and justify whether it is ready to merge.</p></li><li><p>Practical system-design judgment across APIs, SQL, database design, data validation, state management and concurrency where relevant.</p></li><li><p>Strong testing and debugging skills: you choose useful test boundaries, construct representative data and investigate failures.</p></li><li><p>Experience making imperfect operational, machine, sensor or similarly complex data trustworthy, with an interest in its industrial meaning and consequences.</p></li><li><p>Resourcefulness: you learn unfamiliar code and technologies through documentation, small experiments, focused questions and feedback.</p></li><li><p>Clear written and spoken English, constructive collaboration and reliable follow-through.</p></li></ul><p>We welcome different educational and professional paths. Direct manufacturing experience is especially useful; equivalent engineering depth from adjacent domains is also relevant.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Particularly Relevant Experience</strong></p><p>Bring depth in one or more of these areas; expertise in all of them is not expected.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Machine data, analytics and machine learning:</strong> Time-series or sensor-data processing, curation, feature engineering, anomaly detection, condition monitoring or quality prediction. Explain how you handled time