built in service of hospitality first. Thousands of restaurants, cafés, bars, and coffee shops across the Netherlands, UK, Italy, Spain, Germany, Denmark and Finland already love running on Tebi.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a natural Sales person who is passionate about hospitality. Sales is at the heart of our business growth right now, and you will be driving it forward in your day-to-day. This role is about more than closing deals, it is about blending with the hospitality scene and winning the market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your day-to-day you can expect a mix of top of funnel activities, field sales, cold sales, networking, events and more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our sales are not your typical SaaS or office sales. We meet our customers where they operate:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find the coolest new hospitality spots in town that everyone talks about</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create engaging ways to show our product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use creative communication strategies to close the deal that will help the merchant operate smarter</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do a smooth handover to the onboarding team to make sure we go live quickly and successfully</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Efficiently use our CRM and other Sales tools (Hubspot, Clay, AI) to leave more time for creativity and connection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously improve and revisit our sales funnel</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep an eye on the new developments in the industry and the merchants needs to create our own path</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Need</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a natural relationship builder with a passion for hospitality industry:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on approach, independence and hunger for fast-paced operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Natural curiosity and a healthy appetite for calculated risk  - we want you to try new things and not be afraid to fail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong and engaging communication skills - you can grab an attention of a busy hospitality owner and keep them interested</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion and curiosity for hospitality and hospitality tech</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A minimum of 3 years of experience in Sales, Commercial Account Management or Hospitality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous POS/ Hospitality tech sales is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable working in English</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this speaks to you we can be the right fit. Learn more about how we work from our Recipe here:<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers"> <u>https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible time off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team events<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we use AI at Tebi</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and improve but doesn’t make the last call. If there's a smarter way to do something, we want to find it.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tebi/account-executive-london-15768","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794606019},{"slug":"bristol-station-manager-operations-manager-248783","company_name":"Roadsurfer","title":"BRISTOL - Station Manager / Operations Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why roadsurfer?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TEAM SPIRIT &amp; TEAM EVENTS:</strong> Enjoy a friendly atmosphere with flat hierarchies, lots of fun, and great team spirit – plus regular team events like sports sessions, BBQs, or simply an after-work drink at your station.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CAMPER BUDGET:</strong> You’ll receive an annual free rental for our campers so you can experience the #happyroadsurfing lifestyle yourself.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>DISCOUNTS &amp; BENEFITS:</strong> Take advantage of our corporate benefits platform, the Travel Industry Card, and Family &amp; Friends discounts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>DEVELOPMENT &amp; GROWTH:</strong> Growth plays a key role at roadsurfer! At our regular Station Life Camps and Trainings, you can connect with team members from around the world and boost your skills, whether it's about vehicle knowledge or customer service – always guided by our Learning &amp; Training experts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role – Your Passion</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location Development:</strong> Together with central departments and your team, you build and manage the location, ensuring smooth daily operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Optimization:</strong> You implement and improve existing standards and bring in your own ideas – for example, for vehicle handovers and returns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>International Collaboration:</strong> You work closely with roadsurfer teams in other countries to continuously improve processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Leadership:</strong> You lead your team with empathy, clear communication, and a supportive style that creates clarity, drives performance, and helps your team grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Recruitment:</strong> You build your team and find talents who share your enthusiasm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fleet Management:</strong> You keep an overview of the vehicle fleet, ensure its condition, and coordinate with local service partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Care:</strong> You know our products – myroadsurfer, abo, spots, and rent – and provide friendly, competent advice so customers become happy roadsurfers on Europe’s roads.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you need to surf the wave with us</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Successfully completed training or studies in a relevant subject area or comparable qualification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 1–2 years of relevant work experience, preferably in car rental, tourism, or similar – career changers are welcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial experience in team leadership is a plus – what matters most is empathy, good communication skills, and a supportive leadership style that creates clarity, drives performance, and helps your team grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong service and customer focus with a friendly and open attitude.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical and solution-focused mindset with enthusiasm for a varied role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent English skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driver's license Class B.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Salary</strong><br />We ❤️ transparency. The salary range for this position is between 32,000 EUR and 33,600 Pounds gross per year. We are currently introducing salary bands in our job descriptions to ensure that all employees are treated fairly. Once we get to know each other better during the application process and can assess your skills and experience more precisely, we will work together to determine which level within the salary band is the best fit for you. In an annual feedback meeting, your salary will be reviewed at least once a year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to surf?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to receiving your application! If you have any questions, feel free to reach out to us at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- and we will get back to you as soon as possible. Please apply exclusively via our application tool – this ensures nothing gets lost and allows us to process your application quickly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ABOUT #ROADSURFER</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are more than Europe's largest campervan rental company. In 2021 we launched our platform roadsurfer spots in addition to our other products rent, abo and sales – a platform where you can discover and book unique camping spots. But that’s only the beginning. We are growing fast, so hop on board and join us on our journey. The roadsurfer philosophy is simple: rent an RV, start your adventure, be happy. Come ride the wave with us!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/roadsurfer/bristol-station-manager-operations-manager-248783","tags":["Regional Station Management Europe"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Bristol","created_at":1794606017},{"slug":"montu-pharmacy-assessment-centre-winnersh-45927","company_name":"Montu Uk","title":"Montu Pharmacy Assessment Centre","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to start or take the next step in your pharmacy career?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Montu, we are doing things differently, and that includes how we recruit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are growing, and we are looking for enthusiastic, hardworking and patient-focused individuals to join our pharmacy team in Winnersh Triangle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Whether you are looking to take your first step into healthcare, explore a new career in pharmacy or bring your existing pharmacy experience to a rapidly growing organisation, we would love to meet you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hosting a <strong>Pharmacy Assessment Centre on Wednesday 18th November</strong>, giving you the opportunity to experience a different approach to recruitment, demonstrate your skills and learn more about what it is like to work at Montu.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not need previous pharmacy experience for all of our opportunities. For our entry-level positions, what matters most is your attitude, willingness to learn and genuine commitment to making a difference to patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our pharmacy is busy. Really busy. It is a lively, energetic environment where things move quickly, teamwork is essential and no two days are quite the same. If you enjoy being on your feet, working alongside others and being part of a team where everyone has a role to play, you could feel right at home.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behind every prescription we process is a patient relying on us to get things right. Whether you are packing medication, dispensing prescriptions or completing final accuracy checks, your contribution matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Opportunities Available</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are recruiting across several positions within our pharmacy team, with opportunities for both experienced pharmacy professionals and individuals looking to enter the industry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pharmacy Assistant</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An excellent entry point into the pharmacy sector, with no previous pharmacy experience required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will support the day-to-day operations of our busy pharmacy, including preparing orders, packing medication, supporting stock management and helping ensure prescriptions are processed accurately and efficiently.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for individuals who are organised, reliable, comfortable with repetitive tasks and enjoy working in a hands-on, fast-paced environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trainee Pharmacy Dispenser</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Looking to develop a career in pharmacy? This could be your opportunity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">No previous dispensing experience is required. You will receive training and support as you develop the knowledge and practical skills needed to work within our dispensing team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will learn about prescription processing, medication handling, accuracy, pharmacy procedures and the importance of maintaining high standards of patient safety.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pharmacy Dispenser</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For individuals with an existing dispensing qualification and experience working within a pharmacy environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will support the safe and accurate dispensing of prescriptions, working closely with pharmacists, technicians and the wider pharmacy team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will need excellent attention to detail, a strong understanding of pharmacy procedures and the ability to maintain accuracy while managing high prescription volumes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accuracy Checking Dispenser</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for qualified and experienced Accuracy Checking Dispensers who can help maintain the high standards of accuracy and patient safety expected within our pharmacy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will undertake accuracy checking duties within the scope of your qualification, training and authorisation, supporting the efficient processing of prescriptions and working collaboratively with the wider team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accuracy Checking Technician (ACT)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For qualified Pharmacy Technicians with an accredited accuracy checking qualification and current GPhC registration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will play an important role in maintaining dispensing accuracy, supporting pharmacy operations and ensuring our processes meet the required professional and regulatory standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will bring confidence, attention to detail and the ability to work effectively in a high-volume dispensing environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Is Our Pharmacy Assessment Centre?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that traditional interviews do not always give people the best opportunity to demonstrate what they can do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That is why we are taking a slightly different approach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Pharmacy Assessment Centre is designed to be an engaging, practical and interactive experience where you can demonstrate your abilities, meet members of the Montu team and gain a better understanding of our working environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can expect a combination of practical and team-based activities designed to assess skills relevant to working within our pharmacy, including:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Literacy and the ability to follow written instructions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working effectively with others</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organisation and the ability to follow processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speed and efficiency without compromising accuracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communication and problem-solving</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are not expecting everyone to arrive with pharmacy knowledge, particularly those applying for our entry-level opportunities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are interested in how you approach tasks, how you work with others and whether you have the right attitude to succeed in our environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What happens after the assessment centre?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates who successfully complete the assessment centre will be invited to attend a further on-site interview at Montu on a later date.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note that attendance at the assessment centre does not guarantee an interview or offer of employment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Are We Looking For?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for people who genuinely want to be part of a team making a difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ideal candidates will be:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Patient-focused:</strong> You understand that the work you do has a direct impact on the people relying on our service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Detail-oriented:</strong> Accuracy matters, particularly when working with medication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable in a busy environment:</strong> You enjoy an energetic workplace and can remain focused when things get hectic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reliable and hardworking:</strong> You take pride in doing your job well and supporting the people around you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team players:</strong> You understand that pharmacy operations depend on people working together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptable:</strong> You are comfortable learning new processes and responding to change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Eager to learn:</strong> Whether you are new to pharmacy or already experienced, you are motivated to develop your skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not need to be the loudest person in the room or have years of experience to succeed here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What matters is your work ethic, your attention to detail and your commitment to doing things properly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Montu</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Montu is a leading medical cannabis company working to improve access to cannabis-based medicines for patients across the UK.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Through our specialist clinical services and pharmacy operations, we support patients receiving prescribed cannabis-based medicines for a range of eligible medical conditions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our multidisciplinary teams bring together clinicians, pharmacists, pharmacy technicians, dispensers and operational colleagues, all working towards the same goal: delivering safe, effective and patient-centred care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a rapidly growing organisation, and our pharmacy is at the heart of what we do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every prescription represents a patient who is depending on us. From the moment a prescription reaches our pharmacy to the moment medication is dispatched, every member of our team plays an important role in that patient journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are proud to be helping shape an evolving area of healthcare, and we want people who are excited to be part of that journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Join Montu?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Montu means becoming part of a growing organisation where your work has purpose and your contribution makes a difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salaries dependent on the position, qualifications and experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunities for training and professional development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Career progression within our growing pharmacy operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A supportive and collaborative team environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to gain experience within a specialist area of healthcare</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The chance to be part of a growing business helping improve patient access to prescribed medication</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Further information about the benefits applicable to each role will be provided during the recruitment process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to Join Us?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Assessment Centre: Monday 2 November 2026</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location: Winnersh Triangle, Berkshire</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are looking for an opportunity to begin a career in pharmacy, develop your existing skills or take the next step within a growing healthcare organisation, we would love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Apply now to be considered for a place at our Pharmacy Assessment Centre.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Following an initial review of applications, shortlisted candidates will receive further information about the assessment centre, including timings, location details and what to expect on the day.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/montu-uk/montu-pharmacy-assessment-centre-winnersh-45927","tags":["Montu"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Winnersh","created_at":1794606016},{"slug":"remote-anaesthetic-pain-consultant-250308","company_name":"Montu Uk","title":"Anaesthetic (Pain) Consultant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At Montu UK, we are passionate about improving the lives of patients who have often exhausted conventional treatment options. Through our Alternaleaf clinic, we are helping people living with chronic and debilitating conditions access treatments that can make a genuine difference to their quality of life.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for Consultant Anaesthetists who are interested in exploring the growing field of medical cannabis and developing their expertise in chronic pain management.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an exciting opportunity to be part of a rapidly growing healthcare organisation, working alongside a multidisciplinary team of experienced clinicians who share a passion for improving patient outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With a fully funded Postgraduate Diploma in Pain Management and comprehensive specialist training, we are keen to hear from consultants who are open to exploring new approaches to patient care and want to make a meaningful difference in an evolving area of medicine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous chronic pain experience is not essential. What matters is a genuine interest in learning, an open-minded approach to alternative treatment options and a commitment to delivering excellent patient care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What is the job?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Consultant Anaesthetist at Montu, the role focuses on assessing and supporting patients living with chronic pain who may have exhausted conventional treatment options.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working within our Alternaleaf clinic, consultants play a central role in determining the suitability of cannabis-based prescription medicines (CBPMs), developing individualised treatment plans and supporting patients throughout their treatment journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The position offers the opportunity to build on existing expertise in analgesic pharmacology, pain management and opioid stewardship while developing specialist knowledge in an evolving area of medicine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our multidisciplinary approach brings together consultants, nurses, pharmacists and other healthcare professionals, allowing consultants to focus on clinical assessment, prescribing decisions and ongoing patient care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Sponsored Postgraduate Diploma in Pain Management</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of our commitment to clinical development, Montu is offering a <strong>fully funded Postgraduate Diploma in Pain Management through the University of South Wales</strong>, delivered fully online in partnership with Learna.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The programme provides an opportunity to develop specialist knowledge in chronic pain management while continuing to gain practical clinical experience within our multidisciplinary team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the diploma</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A 12-month, part-time postgraduate diploma with all teaching and assessment completed online.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Focuses on interdisciplinary and multidisciplinary pain management, assessment and service provision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full course fees funded by Montu UK.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two hours of protected, paid study time each week.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Further information about the programme is available through the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.southwales.ac.uk/courses/pgdip-pain-management/">University of South Wales</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Eligibility</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A minimum working commitment of 24 hours per week with Montu.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two of those hours each week are allocated as protected, paid study time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continued employment with Montu at a minimum of 24 hours per week for the duration of the diploma.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What will you be doing?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Providing high-quality care for patients seeking medical cannabis treatment for chronic pain and other qualifying conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conducting patient consultations, including clinical assessments, prescribing decisions and ongoing patient management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Applying anaesthetic expertise in analgesic pharmacology, drug interactions and opioid stewardship to support safe prescribing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reviewing patient progress and treatment effectiveness, making adjustments where clinically appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engaging in clinical outcome data collection to support evidence-based practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributing to clinical governance and maintaining robust patient care standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with a multidisciplinary team, including nurses and pharmacists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Completing the sponsored Postgraduate Diploma in Pain Management alongside clinical responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participating in ongoing training and professional development, including specialist training in cannabis-based prescription medicines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you need</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full GMC registration with a current licence to practise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Completion of specialist training in Anaesthesia (CCT/CCST) or equivalent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entry on the GMC Specialist Register for Anaesthesia.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of analgesic pharmacology, pain management and safe prescribing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills and a patient-centred approach to care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work independently while contributing to a multidisciplinary clinical team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong interest in chronic pain and alternative treatment options.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to participate in clinical outcome data collection and reporting.</