pathways from experimentation to larger production workloads.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An experienced product marketer.</strong> You have proven experience in product marketing, growth marketing or developer marketing within B2B technology, developer platforms, APIs or AI, with demonstrable impact on product adoption and commercial outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A strategic storyteller.</strong> You've taken technical products from ambiguity to market, developing differentiated positioning and go-to-market strategies that help products stand out in competitive markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent in developer audiences.</strong> You understand how developers discover, evaluate and adopt technical products, and know how to build trust, reduce friction and drive sustained engagement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technically credible.</strong> You can navigate API documentation, work with sample code and engage confidently with engineers and product teams. You understand the fundamentals of model performance, latency, inference costs, throughput and context windows, and can translate technical complexity into customer value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercially minded and analytical.</strong> You connect marketing strategy to business outcomes, understand product-led growth, monetisation, and sales, and you use data to prioritise investments and measure impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A builder and cross-functional leader.</strong> You thrive in greenfield environments, influence senior stakeholders, challenge assumptions constructively and bring teams together around clear priorities. You're comfortable creating new capabilities and scaling what works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curious.</strong> You 