ically complex products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of developing differentiated product positioning and messaging that translates technical capabilities into clear customer and business value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading product launches and building go-to-market strategies for enterprise technology products, from early positioning through adoption and commercial scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of enterprise buying journeys, including technical evaluation, stakeholder alignment, procurement considerations, and the challenges of deploying new technologies at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to engage credibly with technical audiences while communicating effectively with executive and business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience partnering closely with Product, Engineering, Sales, Solutions, and other cross-functional teams to drive alignment and execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A commercial mindset, with the ability to connect product marketing initiatives to adoption, pipeline development, deal progression, and revenue growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong competitive and market intelligence skills, with the ability to turn customer and market insights into actionable GTM strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for simplifying complex concepts into clear, compelling narratives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on, proactive approach and the ability to operate independently, navigate ambiguity, and build repeatable processes in a fast-moving environment.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience marketing AI platforms, model platforms, cloud infrastructure, or enterprise developer tools.</p></li><li><p style="