<p data-lfile-container="61d171d5-b814-4e82-b6c7-fbf6810c9455" data-pm-slice="1 1 []"><strong>Paris (Office-first)</strong></p>
<h3 id="team-description-1"><strong>Team description</strong></h3>
<p>SumUp already powers over 4 million businesses worldwide. We're now aiming for bigger names, and we're building the team to do it. In France, our Key Account Sales team goes after larger businesses, from hospitality groups to beauty chains and major retailers. You'll choose how you prospect, by phone or in the field, get into their networks and close the deals. As one of the first people on this new team, you'll help work out what it takes to win these accounts, with plenty of opportunities opening up as we grow. The best part? Your variable pay is uncapped, so there's no ceiling on what you can earn.</p>
<h3 id="what-youll-do-1"><strong>What you'll do</strong></h3>
<p>Identify and reach high-potential businesses, such as hospitality groups, beauty chains and major retailers</p>
<p>Run high-volume outreach by phone, in the field and through other channels</p>
<p>Get in front of decision-makers and understand how their business and sites operate</p>
<p>Book meetings and run tailored pitches and demos that show how SumUp can support their business</p>
<p>Own the full sales cycle, from first contact through to closing the deal</p>
<p>Grow your portfolio and network over time, using each win to open the next door</p>
<p>Track your performance against targets and use feedback and data to keep improving</p>
<h3 id="what-were-looking-for-1"><strong>What we're looking for…</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>Proven experience in outbound sales, with a track record of hitting targets</li>
<li>Comfort with high volumes of outreach, by phone or in the field</li>
<li>Real drive and resilience: you stay motivated when deals take time or doors stay closed</li>
<li>Confidence and the ability to build strong relationships with business owners and decision-makers</li>
<li>Comfort with having freedom in how you work, alongside hands-on coaching and support from your team lead</li>
<li>Fluency in French and English</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="why-you-should-join-sumup-1"><strong>Why you should join SumUp</strong></h3>
<p>💰 Uncapped variable pay: strong performance can significantly increase your earnings</p>
<p>🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our Paris location. This involves an office-first setup</p>
<p>🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone's perspectives are respected and embraced</p>
<p>📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;D budget of €2,000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education</p>
<p>💼 Financial security: corporate pension contributions that support your long-term future</p>
<p>🏥 Healthcare support: we cover 50% of the monthly cost of your health insurance for your Mutuelle and Prévoyance</p>
<p>🚌 Extra allowances: we offer restaurant tickets (Swile) and cover transportation costs</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h2><strong>About SumUp</strong></h2>
<p>Be empowered to do more that matters.</p>
<p>At SumUp, we're on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 37 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.</p>
<p>Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI" target="_blank">our diverse team</a> of over 3,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset. <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/" target="_blank">Our core values</a> lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.</p>
<p>SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don't make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.sumup.com/careers/" target="_blank">careers website</a>, and follow our journey on <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>, <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/" target="_blank">Instagram</a>, and <a class="text-primary underline cursor-pointer" href="https://www.tiktok.com/@insidesumup" target="_blank">TikTok</a>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p><div class="content-conclusion"><p><strong>Job Application Tip</strong></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don't tick every box, it's ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.</span></p></div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/sumup/key-account-sales-executive-paris-173927","tags":[],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1794613527},{"slug":"remote-senior-growth-product-manager-paris-473086","company_name":"Soda Data Nv","title":"Senior Growth Product Manager","description":"<p>Data quality is the bottleneck of the AI era. Every Fortune 500 is trying to solve it. We're the team they call.</p><p>Soda is the data quality layer for Disney, Ralph Lauren, CBRE, HelloFresh, 2K Games, and Nubank. Our open-source engine, Soda Core, is used by companies like Tesla, Slack, Adyen, Walmart, and JPMC. The category is growing fast because AI doesn't work on bad data, and we're hiring a <strong>Senior Growth Product Manager</strong> to get customers using Soda faster and on more of their data.</p><h3>About Us</h3><p>Soda's mission is to monitor the world's decisions. We're building the first Data &amp; AI performance monitoring platform that spans data collection to automated decision-making. Soda helps customers find, understand, and fix data quality issues by combining automated post-production monitoring with pre-production pipeline data testing.</p><p>Soda was founded in 2019 by Maarten (employee #5 at Collibra) and Tom (creator of multiple open-source projects generating hundreds of millions in value). We commercialize through Soda Cloud and we're well-funded, with investors like Point 9 Capital, Hummingbird, Singular, and Eurazeo.</p><h3>The Role</h3><p>You'll lead our adoption team, a small group of frontend, full-stack, and AI engineers. The team works on onboarding and activation, on keeping workflows coherent across the product, on customer-facing dashboards, and on AI features that save users work.</p><p>Most of our roadmap is driven by what customers and prospects ask for. This team's work is driven by adoption metrics, because customers rarely ask for the things that would make them use Soda more. You'll start from a hypothesis, for example that changing a flow will get 20% more data contracts created, ship the change, and check whether it worked.</p><p>We sell to enterprises, so sample sizes are small and A/B tests rarely reach significance. You'll use product analytics, session replays, and conversations with users, and you'll often have to decide with incomplete data. This is a product role. If most of your growth experience is in paid acquisition or lifecycle email, it's probably the wrong fit. You'll also work closely with our Growth team, which is led by a co-founder, on launches and messaging.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul><li>Own the adoption metrics for Soda Cloud: time to first verified contract for new accounts, data coverage (datasets with contracts and monitors), weekly active datasets and users, and usage of AI features. You'll define them, make sure we can measure them, and improve them.</li><li>Own the UX of workflows across the product and keep them coherent for our two kinds of users: data engineers, and business users such as data stewards and governance leads.</li><li>Find where customers get stuck between signing the contract and running Soda on most of their data, and decide what to fix first.</li><li>Design and ship onboarding flows that get a new team to first value within days, including self-serve paths for technical teams that want to evaluate Soda on their own.</li><li>Put AI to work on adoption: decide which steps an agent should do for the user, ship them with the team, and measure whether people keep using them.</li><li>Work with Growth on launches and product marketing, and with our customer engineers on whatever is blocking rollouts at customers.</li></ul><h3>Hiring Process</h3><ol><li>Application: your CV, plus a short answer about one metric you moved (what it was, what you shipped, what happened, and what didn't work)</li><li>15-minute phone screen</li><li>First interview (60 min): a deep dive into product growth work you've done. Part of it is showing us something you shipped that you'd still be proud to demo.</li><li>Second interview (60 min): a working session on a real Soda adoption problem</li><li>Culture fit (45 min)</li></ol><p>We answer every application, and every candidate hears back within 3–5 days of each step. If it's not a hell yes, it's a no, and we'll tell you quickly and kindly.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h3>You Should Have</h3><ul><li><strong>5+ years in product, including at least 2 owning growth, activation, onboarding, or adoption in B2B SaaS</strong>: you were accountable for a metric for long enough to see whether your changes worked. In your application, tell us which metric it was, where it started and where it ended, what you shipped, and what didn't work.</li><li><strong>Product craft and taste</strong>: you love software and have used a lot of it yourself, so you know what a good product feels like. You keep scope small, work in short cycles with engineers and designers, run your own customer calls, and have well-reasoned opinions about UX.</li><li><strong>An AI-native way of working and building</strong>: you've shipped an AI-powered feature and measured whether people use it, you prototype with coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, etc.), and you're happy to open a small PR yourself for something like a copy change.</li><li><strong>You do your own analysis</strong>: you write SQL, build funnels yourself, and know when a sample is too small to conclude anything.</li><li><strong>Experience with technical products</strong>: you've built for engineers or data teams and are comfortable talking about pipelines, warehouses, and APIs.</li><li><strong>Clear writing and comfort working async</strong>: we're a distributed team across 12+ countries, and most decisions happen in writing, in English.</li></ul><p>The five years don't all have to be in a PM role. If you were a product engineer or a founder and owned a growth metric, please apply.</p><h3>Good to Have</h3><ul><li>Data quality, data observability, data governance, or data infrastructure experience.</li><li>Experience with product-led growth at a company that also sells to enterprises.</li><li>Experience with Shape Up or another fixed-time, variable-scope way of working.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul><li>Compensation €120,000–140,000/year + equity.</li><li>Outside Belgium, this is a contractor position.</li><li>Fully remote (EU-based), with a Belgian office available if you want one.</li><li>In-person kickoffs every two months in cool locations across Europe, three days with the whole product and engineering team.</li><li>All the tokens you need, across all frontier models.</li><li>Real ownership, real impact, no micromanagement.</li><li>A senior team that ships, across 12+ countries.</li></ul><h3>Our Values</h3><p>We value freedom with responsibility, transparency, and a growth mindset. We avoid politics, have no tolerance for dishonesty, and value open and direct communication without judgment. We proactively bring up and address potential issues before they become critical, and we overcommunicate frequently. Working at Soda, you will have full autonomy to make impactful product and roadmap decisions.</p><h3>❤️ Why you will love to join Soda</h3><ul><li><strong>You own the adoption metrics</strong>: you decide how we measure adoption and what we do to improve it.</li><li><strong>Lots of room to improve</strong>: we already have enterprise customers and usage data, and we've done very little growth work so far.</li><li><strong>Your own engineering team</strong>: you'll work with dedicated engineers who build agentically, so your ideas get shipped quickly.</li><li><strong>Be part of a transformation</strong>: data quality is having its moment, and we're at the front of it.</li><li><strong>Work on your own terms</strong>: fully remote, flexible hours, colleagues in 12+ countries.</li></ul><h3>😡 What you might not love</h3><ul><li><strong>Rapidly changing priorities</strong>: our roadmap can pivot quickly. It's a fast-paced environment with a LOT of work to be done.</li><li><strong>Small numbers</strong>: we have relatively few accounts and feedback is slow. If you're used to deciding from consumer-scale data, you may find that frustrating.</li><li><strong>No playbook</strong>: this is the first dedicated growth PM role at Soda.</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/soda-data-nv/remote-senior-growth-product-manager-paris-473086","tags":["Computer Software","Product and Engineering","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1794612009},{"slug":"digital-marketing-manager-paris-cdd-9months-118087","company_name":"mirakl","title":"Digital Marketing Manager, Paris - CDD 9months","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mirakl:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2012, Mirakl has been at the forefront of marketplace innovation, empowering every business to compete in the platform economy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Today, Mirakl’s operating system combines an enterprise marketplace solution (Mirakl Platform) that enables retailers and B2B organizations to launch, scale, and operate marketplaces and dropship, AI-powered multichannel selling (Mirakl Connect), retail media (Mirakl Ads) and an agentic commerce infrastructure (Mirakl Nexus).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With dual headquarters in Boston and Paris, Mirakl helps a global ecosystem of 450+ marketplaces (B2C and B2B) and a network of over 100k third-party marketplace sellers. Brands like Macy’s, Decathlon, Carrefour, Asos, and Airbus Helicopters use Mirakl to grow their businesses in new and remarkable ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mirakl.com&quot;&gt;www.mirakl.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mirakl in Numbers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
