o We Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Building the AI-first frontier enterprise.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a global technology consultancy with a trademarked, AI-first approach<strong>—Gen-e2™. </strong>It redefines how enterprises build digital products and transform their organizations with AI. <strong>We do the right thing, and we do it right.</strong> We're proud to be a World Economic Forum New Champion, and a B Corp-certified company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· We are small enough to care locally, big enough to deliver globally (<strong>10 countries, 450+ experts from 50+ nationalities</strong>)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· We are becoming an <strong>agentic organization</strong>, adopting the AI-native operating model we bring to our clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· We are<strong> robust and resilient </strong>(100% independent, 0 debt, founded 2009)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· We are <strong>AI-native professionals </strong>who invest in what we believe and work as a collective intelligence</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· We are positive, courageous and deliver at the leading edge</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>🚀 Your Role</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">For our PALO IT LABS based in Paris, 17e District, and entirely focused on developing our Gen-e2 methodology, you will use advanced AI tools to accelerate development cycles and drive innovation.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a key member of our team, driven by Sami Henchiri, you will lead high-impact, AI-driven engineering initiatives and transformation programs from discovery to delivery. You will be responsible for technical excellence, and client success, ensuring each project aligns with the Gen-e2 speed-to-impact model.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your soft skills will help you build or be part of a high-performing team that consistently exceeds expectations by effectively blending human expertise and AI capabilities.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>🎯 Your Mission</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a AI Native Coach Transformation, your mission is both internal and external:</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead multidisciplinary engineering and product teams</strong>, delivering large-scale, AI-driven, cloud-native solutions integrating DevSecOps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define technical strategy</strong>, support clients in transformative adoption of fully AI-driven delivery models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct technical analyses, define solution architectures, and facilitate client workshops to determine project technical approaches</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Implement Gen-e2 best practices</strong>, from product repository artifacts to AI prompt libraries for coding standards, architecture, and security compliance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Train and coach client teams on Gen-e</strong>2, enabling them to adopt AI-driven ways of working and anchor them in their culture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support organizations in scaling Gen-e2, by <strong>creating strategies and frameworks for enterprise-wide adoption</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Boost productivity and quality by leveraging AI to generate the majority of artifacts while applying rigorous review and validation processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Foster an AI-First engineering culture</strong>, mentoring teams to master AI-First practices in research, design, prototyping, backlog creation, and code generation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously experiment with practices and improve our delivery approach, leveraging the latest AI capabilities, tools, and patterns to push product engineering boundaries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage stakeholders, ensuring delivery at least 50% faster than client expectations</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>You’re in the right place if:</h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have proven leadership in engineering/consulting and have coached teams and enabled clients (transformations, playbooks) in demanding agile environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a solid grounding in software engineering, design/architecture, and know how to move from discovery to delivery with impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You master AI code assistants (Copilot, Cursor, etc.), prompt engineering, and have a passion for reinventing a measured AI-First SDLC (DORA, quality, SLOs).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have expertise in cloud &amp; platform (AWS/Azure, GCP+), serverless, Kubernetes, IaC (Terraform/CDK), CI/CD, trunk-based, observability (OTel, Prom/Grafana), and security by design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable with enterprise tooling/migration (Atlassian, Azure DevOps, GitHub Enterprise, SSO, GDPR) and can navigate stakeholders (CTO/CIO/CISO, Product, Data, Legal) with business alignment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a builder spirit, service-oriented leadership, clear communication, and are comfortable with innovation, ambiguity, and change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are sensitive to Tech for Good (B Corp)—accessibility, sustainability, AI ethics—and fluent English (other languages are a plus).</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our consultants’ profiles are all diverse, and we are proud of this richness. Don’t hesitate to contact us if your profile does not meet 100% of this posting, we also value:</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharing your commitment, technical knowledge, willingness, and enthusiasm in conferences or development and Software Craftsmanship communities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participation in one or more Open Source projects as a contributor, for example</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your passion for eco-design, modern social challenges, innovation in human fields, and sustainable development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your engagement in associations or meetups around people and the environment</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>What we offer you</h1><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A playground matching your expertise: missions chosen for their complexity, engineering requirements, and business/social impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A dedicated career coach who guides you with regular sessions to structure, monitor, and accelerate your development goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A demanding and caring technical community: code reviews, pair programming, sharing, and mentoring to continuously raise the bar for craft and rigor</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gen-e2 skills development paths from week 1 and throughout your onboarding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Microsoft and GitHub certifications funded from onboarding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">From idea to sharing: internal R&amp;D lab, open source by default, tech conferences, and innovation dojos to experiment, code, and transmit</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>But also</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 Global career, multi-sector and potentially multi-country missions, bridges between 10 offices</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏠 Remote Friendly depending on the project, with onsite days at client premises or in our offices at République, Paris, with team meetings to share and innovate</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌱 Impact Academy: climate, responsible digital, and accessibility training integrated into our practices</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 Solidarity involvement: team volunteering, skills sponsorship</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥗🩺 Swile for meal vouchers, Alan for great health coverage</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At PALO IT, diversity is a source of innovation and impact. As a B Corp, we offer equal opportunities and assess candidates only on their skills, potential, and motivation. We welcome applications without discrimination based on gender identity/expression, sexual orientation, age, origin, ethnicity, religion, disability, or any other protected attribute.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/palo-it/ai-native-coach-transformation-paris-260199","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"PALO IT France","created_at":1794606018},{"slug":"senior-revenue-operations-manager-paris-361885","company_name":"Lemlist","title":"Senior Revenue Operations Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">lemlist is the outbound platform for sales teams: find leads, run multichannel campaigns (email, LinkedIn, calls), personalize with AI and book meetings.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">lempire also builds lemwarm (deliverability), Claap (AI call intelligence), Taplio and Tweet Hunter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're at +$60M ARR, growing ~50% year over year, profitable and 100% bootstrapped, with 180 people.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your mission</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">lemlist and Claap sell through several motions at once: self-serve, sales-led, account management and partners. More than a quarter of our ARR sits in 1,200+ accounts managed by our Customer Success and Account Management teams. In 2027, these teams start working the same portfolio under a new customer segmentation, and expanding our existing accounts, including cross-selling Claap and our new products, is one of our biggest bets of the year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Senior Revenue Operations Manager (Customer Ops), your mission is to design how our revenue motions run, and own the systems and data behind them. In the short term, your focus is customer operations, from the moment Sales hands over an account to every renewal and expansion. Over time, the role can evolve toward Sales ops, Partnerships or other revenue topics, depending on your strengths, your interests and company priorities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join our Finance &amp; Operations team, six people today, and report to Philippe, Head of Finance &amp; Operations. Your main stakeholders are the leaders of Customer Experience, Account Management, Sales and Partnerships.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role. You'll spend most of your time in HubSpot, our customer tools, automations and dashboards, building things people use every day. You also bring the business view: you know your numbers better than anyone, and you turn them into clear recommendations for the teams you work with.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Where you'll make an impact</h2><h3>Your first focus: customers</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Give customer teams one view of every account.</strong> Bring product usage, billing and CRM data together, so every account tells the full story in one place. Own the build-or-buy decision on our customer platform, lead the rollout, and build with the Data team the dashboards that make CSMs' day-to-day easier and give leadership clear visibility on the customer base.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build our risk detection engine.</strong> Turn usage, payment and engagement signals into early alerts across the whole portfolio, from our largest accounts with a dedicated CSM to the ones we manage at scale, so teams act on churn risk weeks before a renewal.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make renewals and NRR predictable.</strong> With our VP CX and Account Management leaders, build the renewal and NRR forecast leadership can rely on, at least two quarters ahead, and know which accounts will grow, stay or churn.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn our customer base into expansion revenue.</strong> Give Account Managers and CSMs the signals and pipeline to upsell and cross-sell Claap and our new products, and track what it brings.</p><h3>Also in your scope</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alongside customer ops, you'll contribute to the rest of our RevOps work:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales:</strong> make selling lemlist, Claap and new products simple for our reps, with lead routing, pipeline and performance tracking, and clear rules of engagement between Sales, Account Management and partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partners:</strong> make partner deals easy to track, credit and pay, from PartnerStack to the CRM, so the Partnerships team can scale its programs in Europe and the US.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems:</strong> keep CRM and revenue data reliable as we add products, run commission plans people trust, and replace manual work with automations and AI agents.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What success looks like</h2><h3>Within your first 3 months</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've audited our customer motion and shared a 12-month plan with Philippe, our VP CX and Account Management leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The customer platform decision is made, based on your recommendation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A first version of the churn risk alerts is live for CSMs.</p></li></ul><h3>Within 12 months</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CSMs and Account Managers work from one view of every account, with usage, billing and CRM data they trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Churn risks are flagged weeks ahead, and teams act on them before the renewal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership plans on your renewal and NRR forecast</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've turned the CRM into an expansion and pipeline generation tool, across lemlist and Claap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work contributes to a measurable lift in net revenue retention (NRR) on the managed portfolio.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sales and Partnerships see the difference too: clear rules of engagement, reliable routing, and partner deals credited and paid on time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in RevOps or GTM Ops in B2B SaaS, ideally PLG + SLG.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've owned customer operations for a portfolio at scale (health scores, churn risk, renewal forecasting), and led at least one big change: a tool rollout, a new coverage model or a new customer segmentation. Sales or partner ops experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on CRM admin experience (HubSpot)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with a customer platform (Gainsight, ChurnZero, Planhat or similar) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business sense: you turn data into a recommendation and defend it with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're used to working with VPs and the C-level, and you don't need a brief to start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Builder mindset: you automate, use AI daily, document what you build and close what you start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent French and English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you read <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://lemlist.com/join-lemlist">our values</a> and thought "this is 100% me", you'll thrive in this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What is in it for you</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A senior role with real ownership in a small team: you shape how a $60M+ ARR company sells and grows its customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the customer ops function</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct work with VPs, the COO and the CEO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI by default: we already run AI agents on our CRM and internal tools, and we expect you to reach for AI first in everything you build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profitable, bootstrapped and growing 40+% a year: you build for growth without fundraising pressure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote-friendly, async culture, with a Paris office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Recruitment process</h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with Victoire (Lead TA).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with Oriane (COO).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business case (async) and live debrief with Philippe (Head of Finance &amp; Operations) and Guillaume (VP Customer).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final interview with Charles (CEO).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reference checks and offer.</p></li></ol><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lemlist/senior-revenue-operations-manager-paris-361885","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794606017},{"slug":"bdr-intern-paris-58298","company_name":"Lemlist","title":"BDR intern","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">lemlist is the AI-powered sales engagement platform helping sales teams build pipeline smarter, not harder.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bootstrapped from day one, we've grown from 0 to <strong>$60M+ ARR</strong> in 8 years without raising a single dollar. Today, <strong>40,000+ sales teams</strong> use lemlist to book more meetings and close more deals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building the next generation of outbound: AI-first, multi-channel, highly personalized, and deeply integrated into the way modern sales teams work. And we're just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We're looking for a native English-speaking BDR Intern to help accelerate our international growth.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This internship is perfect for someone starting their sales career and looking for an environment where they can learn incredibly fast. You don't need years of experience. What matters most:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">motivation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">energy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">communication skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">resilience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">willingness to learn</p></li></