ort organization.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be equally comfortable coaching a team member through a customer issue, investigating an API error, improving a support workflow, and partnering with Engineering or Product to address a recurring problem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><br /><strong>Lead frontline support delivery</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach, and develop a distributed L1 Product Support team, providing regular feedback and supporting technical growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own day-to-day L1 Product Support delivery, including queue prioritization, backlog management, customer communication, and regional handoffs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and maintain clear ownership of L1 Product Support queues and handoffs to L2, including for paid self-serve and first-level enterprise requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor service quality, response and resolution times, backlog health, and customer satisfaction; turn insights into practical improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay hands-on with complex or sensitive customer issues and model strong technical judgment.</p></li></ul><h3><br /><strong>Increase Product Support (L1) technical autonomy</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train and coach Product Support (L1) agents to investigate, reproduce, and resolve more technical issues across Mistral products, including Vibe, Studio, and APIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with L2 to identify issue types that Product Support (L1) can safely take on and define the knowledge, access, and safeguards needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create playbooks, troubleshooting guides, and escalation criteria that help Product Support (L1) agents resolve issues independently and consistently.</p></li><li><p style="min-heig