 implementation decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow the engineers, not just the software — set the standard for ownership and coach people past their comfort zone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own people management for the team: hiring, performance, growth paths, and honest feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Managers to turn frontier research needs into shippable primitives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3+ years of real people leadership.</strong> You have managed engineers — hired, coached, given honest feedback, and grown them. Hands-on contribution matters here, but this role is judged on the team you build and lead, not just the code you write.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep Linux internals: namespaces, cgroups, seccomp, virtualization — ideally microVMs of the Firecracker class.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have shipped production systems in Go. Not dabbled. Shipped.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand network isolation at the packet level — not just firewall rules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performance instincts: you know what a syscall costs, and you have the profiles to prove you've cared.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years building backend or infrastructure systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have partnered with product, design, and business teams to ship software that reached real users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A low-ego, team-first mindset. We care less about your exact domain and more about whether you are the kind of technical force other engineers want to work alongside.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth,