&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the country of employment without employer sponsorship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/precisionmedicinegroup/remote-senior-people-operations-partner-259706","tags":["Precision for Medicine"],"job_types":[],"location":"Remote","created_at":1794585320},{"slug":"senior-key-accounts-manager-paris-463364","company_name":"airbnb","title":"Senior Key Accounts Manager","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence, and guest-centered ethos that define Airbnb. This team’s mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping hotels easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;As a Senior Key Account Manager on the Hotels Enterprise team, you will own the commercial relationship with a portfolio of global and multinational hotel groups in your region. Your goal is to turn introductions into signed agreements then into live, healthy, growing inventory by increasing participation, bookings and revenue across Airbnb and HotelTonight. You will lead the account planning cycle with each partner, negotiate and renew commercial terms, and be the single point of contact between their executives and many Airbnb teams including Connectivity, Product, Legal and Market Management teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for the end-to-end lifecycle from prospecting, to acquisition, contracting, rollout and performance management&amp;nbsp; of Key Account partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute a global win-win strategy for your portfolio that drives value to all parties and position Airbnb as a top strategic partner across all distribution channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Through the creation of mutual account plans with your partners you will design clear actions which deliver on the Objectives and KPIs of Airbnb and our Key Account Partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate agreements with partners to unlock new opportunities for both parties &amp;amp; promote long term mutual success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data to make decisions and design projects to best expand and enhance availability and revenue through existing partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor &amp;amp; analyze over/underperformance, market trends, growth opportunities or anomalies and regularly communicate performance to Executives leveraging available production data and global market insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with partners to ensure that the partnership is held to the highest industry standards and that commercial agreements as well as operational SLAs are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop close working relationships with key internal teams and individuals to ensure that they&amp;nbsp; provide appropriate levels of support to these key partnerships and key enhancements are made to unlock revenue for the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular business reviews, formal presentations for internal and external purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to execute changes at scale while collaborating with Market Management as a subject matter expert in Key Accounts accounts to drive local property performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively contribute to the development and standardization of Enterprise team processes, playbooks, and best practices across the global function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of Travel IndustryAccount Management experience; including 5 years in a Key Account Manager role with at least 2 years&amp;nbsp; being responsible for a global partner base.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of executing on strategic priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in analyzing, structuring and negotiating complex deals that align across multiple business unit needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skills with a proven ability to structure and close high-value, complex deals that establish long-term, strategic partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable performing data analysis and making decisions based on the results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance time spent between strategic initiatives and operations while diving into the details when necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and selling complex business solutions at the C-Suite level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and the ability to effectively influence top leaders internally and within the industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a passion for redefining travel, Airbnb, and being the best!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive self-starter able to prioritize and manage work autonomously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal/written communication and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel at least 50% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€74.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€92.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/airbnb/senior-key-accounts-manager-paris-463364","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794585318},{"slug":"sales-development-representative-inbound-villeneuve-dascq-212091","company_name":"Kestra Technologies","title":"Sales Development Representative (Inbound)","description":"<h3><strong>About Kestra</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kestra is the <strong>universal orchestration platform</strong>: open source, declarative, &amp; designed to orchestrate data pipelines, IT automation, business workflows, &amp; AI/agentic systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trusted by <strong>over 10,000 organizations worldwide</strong>, including <strong>JPMorgan Chase, Bloomberg, FILA, &amp; Crédit Agricole</strong>, Kestra orchestrates mission-critical workloads at scale. The open-source project has close to <strong>30,000 GitHub stars</strong>, hundreds of contributors, &amp; a fast-growing global community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About The Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most of Kestra's pipeline starts with someone who already found us: a demo request, a Kestra Cloud trial, a webinar sign-up, or an engineer from the open-source community who wants to talk to Sales. We sell <strong>Kestra Enterprise</strong>, self-hosted in the customer's own infrastructure, &amp; <strong>Kestra Cloud</strong>, our fully managed edition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for our <strong>first inbound Sales Development Representative in Europe</strong> to turn that interest into qualified pipeline. You follow up on every inbound lead, qualify it honestly against our Ideal Customer Profile, &amp; pass it to the right Account Executive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You work closely with our Lead Growth Engineering team</strong>, who build &amp; run the systems that capture, score, &amp; route our inbound demand. Together you decide which signals matter, tighten routing, &amp; make sure no good lead goes cold. You report to the Head of Sales &amp; hand off daily to our European Account Executives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your buyers are technical: data engineers, platform engineers, &amp; the leaders who run those teams. <strong>You don't need to be an engineer, but you need to be curious enough to learn the product &amp; talk credibly about orchestration.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Follow-up</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Every inbound lead routed to you</strong>: demo &amp; contact requests, Kestra Cloud trials &amp; sign-ups, event &amp; webinar follow-ups, &amp; community hand-raises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speed to lead</strong>: a first personal reply within 1 business hour, &amp; at least 4 follow-up attempts over 7 business days before closing a lead out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Messages that read like a person wrote them</strong>: short, relevant, &amp; clearly based on what the prospect actually asked for.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualification</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualification calls</strong> that uncover the prospect's use case, current tooling (Airflow, cron, homegrown scripts, cloud-native schedulers), team, &amp; timeline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Honest qualification</strong> against our Ideal Customer Profile: a real business pain Kestra solves, &amp; someone involved in evaluating or buying.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clean disqualification</strong>: leads that don't fit go back to nurture with a clear reason, so the team learns which sources bring good demand.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hand-off to Account Executives</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Routing each qualified lead to the right Account Executive</strong> by territory &amp; segment, or to the account owner when there is already an open opportunity or an existing customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First meetings that actually happen</strong>, with a written brief so the prospect never has to repeat themselves.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accurate records in HubSpot</strong>: every lead, call, &amp; disqualification reason logged, so forecasts &amp; routing can be trusted.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnership with Lead Growth Engineering</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feedback on lead quality</strong> by source, campaign, &amp; persona, so scoring &amp; routing keep improving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shaping the inbound playbook</strong>: qualification questions, templates, objection handling, &amp; the hand-off checklist.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Spotting gaps early</strong>: leads routed to the wrong place, signals the system misses, or steps that slow a prospect down.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1+ year as an SDR, BDR, or in a similar customer-facing role</strong>, ideally at a B2B SaaS or software company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Inbound experience</strong>: you have worked a lead queue against response-time targets &amp; know how to qualify without losing a good prospect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curiosity about technical products</strong>: you enjoy learning how software works &amp; can hold a credible conversation with an engineer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear, concise writing</strong>: your emails get answered.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CRM discipline</strong>: you keep records accurate because you know other people rely on them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English; a second European language (especially French or German) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working autonomously in a fully remote team, with working hours that cover European business hours.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation, performance bonus, &amp; equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical, dental, &amp; vision insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employer-paid life &amp; disability insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fully remote, with home-office &amp; equipment budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning &amp; conference budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid time off, company holidays, &amp; parental leave</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Location</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Europe</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/kestra-technologies/sales-development-representative-inbound-villeneuve-dascq-212091","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Europe","created_at":1794584418},{"slug":"ai-applied-scientist-paris-27948","company_name":"MakiPeople","title":"AI Applied Scientist","description":"<div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About the Science and AI Team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Science and AI team is at the heart of Maki People. It builds the science and AI behind our platform, from job analysis and assessments to AI interviews and predicting performance. Led by our Head of Science, Aiden Loe, and working closely with our COO, Paul-Louis Caylar, the team brings together business psychologists, psychometricians and AI scientists. Together, they make sure every hiring decision on our platform is accurate, consistent and fair. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Maki grows, the Science and AI team’s job is to show, with evidence, that our approach leads to better hiring decisions.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The AI Applied Scientist turns our science into results for clients. Most of your time goes on client projects: adapting our AI scoring to each client’s roles, analysing their data, and showing them what it means. The rest goes on improving the scoring systems that every client relies on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1. Client projects</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adapt AI scoring for structured interviews, job-specific skills and multilingual proficiency to each client’s roles and needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyse client assessment and performance data to show how scores relate to job performance and retention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set and review cut-offs and thresholds with clients, backed by evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Present findings and recommendations directly to clients, in a way non-technical audiences can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with implementation and customer success teams from setup to go-live.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2. Testing scoring quality</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compare AI scores with expert ratings to check accuracy and reliability before anything goes live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test robustness to prompt variation, input noise and adversarial behaviour such as prompt injection.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3. Fairness in practice</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run bias checks across demographic groups for each client project.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply mitigation techniques such as reweighting and calibration without losing model performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support fairness reports and compliance documentation for clients.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>4. Improving our scoring systems</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help choose the right models and prompts for production, balancing accuracy, speed and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the move onto self-hosted open-weight models, including fine-tuning on expert-rated data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with engineering to roll out scoring changes safely.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As one of Maki People’s early employees, you’ll help shape the team’s future.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Our Ideal Candidate</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Required</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc or PhD in data science, machine learning, psychology or a related field, or equivalent industry experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with LLM-based scoring or evaluation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Python or R skills, with solid statistical analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience presenting data-driven findings to clients or senior business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to manage several projects at once and keep to deadlines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preferred</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in consulting, people analytics or assessment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of psychometric concepts such as reliability, validity and IRT.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience testing AI systems for fairness and bias.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience fine-tuning language models, for example with LoRA.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of ethical AI and compliance, such as the EU AI Act.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 1 - Screening assessment (25 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 2 - Power skill assessment with our AI agent (15 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 3 - Hiring manager interview (45 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 4 - Executive interview (45 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 5 - Deep-dive technical interview (60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 6 - Interview with Co-founder (30 min)</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/makipeople/ai-applied-scientist-paris-27948","tags":["Science"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794584418},{"slug":"ai-research-scientist-paris-149972","company_name":"MakiPeople","title":"AI Research Scientist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Science and AI Team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Science and AI team is at the heart of Maki People. It builds the science and AI behind our platform, from job analysis and assessments to AI interviews and predicting performance. Led by our Head of Science, Aiden Loe, and working closely with our COO, Paul-Louis Caylar, the team brings together business psychologists, psychometricians and AI scientists. Together, they make sure every hiring decision on our platform is accurate, consistent and fair. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Maki grows, the Science and AI team’s job is to show, with evidence, that our approach leads to better hiring decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The AI Research Scientist works at the intersection of AI, psychometrics and research, ensuring that Maki’s automated scoring systems are scientifically robust, fair, and continuously improving.</p><h3></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1. Evaluating and testing LLMs for scoring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess the accuracy and reliability of LLMs used for automated scoring, such as structured grids, job-specific skills and multilingual proficiency (written and spoken).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmark closed- and open-source models across assessment types and languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test robustness to prompt variation, input noise and adversarial behaviour such as prompt injection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore prompt engineering and model optimisation, and recommend which models and prompts go into production.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2. Building our own scoring models</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Move our scoring onto self-hosted open-weight models, and fine-tune them on expert-rated data where they can beat frontier models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check every model switch keeps accuracy, reliability and fairness at least as good as today's.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3. Comparing AI with human judgement, and calibrating psychometric models</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design studies that compare AI scores with expert ratings, against both individual experts and expert averages, to establish agreement and validity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop hybrid scoring pipelines with engineering that combine human oversight with AI scoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate and calibrate psychometric models for validity and comparability across populations and test forms.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>4. Bias and fairness analysis</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Detect and analyse bias in AI-generated and psychometric scores across demographic groups, including subgroup analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply mitigation techniques such as reweighting and calibration without losing model performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to fairness dashboards and compliance documentation that support transparent model governance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5. Predictive analytics and performance insights</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model the relationship between candidate scores and job performance and retention, using large assessment and performance datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and test models that estimate success probabilities or identify behavioural and linguistic predictors of performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with data science, implementation and customer success teams to turn findings into recommendations for clients and colleagues.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>6. Research output</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Publish reports, papers and conference presentations, internal and external.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explain technical findings clearly to non-technical colleagues and clients.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>As one of Maki People's early employees, you'll help shape the team's future. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Ideal Candidate</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PhD or MSc in machine learning, computational linguistics, data science or psychology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of publications, such as peer-reviewed papers or conference papers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience evaluating LLMs: designing benchmarks, measuring agreement with human raters, and testing consistency and robustness of model output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience testing AI-driven decisions for fairness and bias.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Python or R, with experience in statistical analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication of results to scientific and business audiences.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with NLP techniques for automated scoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience fine-tuning language models, for example with LoRA.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with cloud databases and large datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of psychometric concepts such as reliability, validity and IRT, and how they apply to assessment design and validation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of ethical AI, data governance and compliance, such as the EU AI Act.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with engineering, product and content teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Application Process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 1 - Screening assessment (25 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 2 - Power skill assessment with our AI agent (15 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 3 - Hiring manager interview (45 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 4 - Executive interview (45 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 5 - Deep-dive technical interview (60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 6 - Interview with Co-founder (30 min)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/makipeople/ai-research-scientist-paris-149972","tags":["Science"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1794584418},{"slug":"sales-development-representative-sdr-saas-sante-paris-329248","company_name":"Lifen","title":"Sales Development Representative (SDR) - Saas Santé","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Chez Lifen, nous pensons que les données médicales ont le potentiel de transformer le système de santé. Mais seulement si elles sont accessibles. Plus de données accessibles → moins de charge administrative, une meilleure coordination des soins et des découvertes scientifiques plus rapides.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depuis 2015, notre mission est de libérer ce potentiel. Nos solutions basées sur l'IA permettent aux professionnels de santé de partager les informations médicales sans effort et aux chercheurs d'accélérer les découvertes cliniques : avec un impact sur des millions de patients en France chaque jour. Alors que nous nous préparons à nous développer en Europe, 2 choses déterminent notre succès : nos équipes et notre mission.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aujourd'hui, plus de 150 personnes travaillent depuis nos bureaux et à distance pour libérer le potentiel des données de santé. Nous avons connecté 800 hôpitaux et 150 000 professionnels de santé, et nous ne faisons que commencer. Nous recherchons des personnes qui embrassent la complexité, veulent résoudre des problèmes difficiles et sont prêtes à construire le futur de la collaboration en santé.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>⚡ <strong>Notre équipe Sales Public</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">L’équipe Sales Public accompagne les établissements de santé dans l’adoption des solutions Lifen, principalement autour de la gestion des documents de santé. Elle compte aujourd’hui 8 Sales Account Executive qui travaillent sur l’ensemble du territoire.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Les Sales concentrent aujourd’hui leur temps sur les plus grands établissements et groupements hospitaliers. À côté, il existe un vivier d’environ 800 structures de santé de plus petite taille.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nous créons donc notre premier poste de SDR Public. Ton rôle sera de construire ce périmètre : mieux connaître ces structures, trouver les personnes à contacter, qualifier les opportunités et transmettre aux Sales des rendez-vous réellement exploitables. Tu travailleras principalement sur nos offres Lifen Documents et Curecall by Lifen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>🎯 Ce que tu feras chez nous</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prioriser un portefeuille d’environ 800 petites structures de santé déjà cartographiée.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrer en contact avec les prospects, comprendre leur contexte et qualifier les opportunités avant de proposer un échange avec un ou une Sales Account Executive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Générer des rendez-vous qualifiés pour l’équipe Sales, en transmettant les informations utiles pour permettre une prise de relais efficace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mettre à jour le CRM avec rigueur : contacts, informations sur les structures, niveau de maturité des opportunités et prochaines étapes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Faire progresser les méthodes de prospection sur ce nouveau périmètre : messages, séquences, critères de qualification et priorisation des comptes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>⭐️ Ce que nous recherchons</strong></h2><h3>Must-have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une première expérience de cold call intensive (Stage, Alternance ou CDI), idéalement d’un à deux ans en startup, en SDR, Inside Sales, prospection B2B ou relation client.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une vraie appétence pour la prospection : prendre contact, obtenir les bonnes informations, relancer et transformer une approche en rendez-vous qualifié.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">La capacité à organiser un volume important de comptes, à prioriser et à tenir un suivi précis dans un CRM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une communication orale et écrite claire, adaptée à des interlocuteurs de direction de structures de santé.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice-to-have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une expérience dans la santé ou auprès de professionnels et d’établissements de santé.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">La pratique d’outils de CRM et de prospection.</p></li></ul><h3>Soft skills</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tu es énergique et tu aimes avancer sur un périmètre à construire. Tu communiques simplement, tu écoutes avant de proposer un rendez-vous et tu acceptes les retours pour ajuster ta manière de faire. L’humilité compte : tu travailleras avec une équipe Sales expérimentée et tu sauras apprendre à ses côtés tout en apportant tes propres observations du terrain.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Nos valeurs</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embrace Complexity</strong>. Tu avances dans un secteur de santé complexe et sur un portefeuille encore peu structuré, en transformant progressivement des informations éparses en opportu