ou we can be the right fit. Learn more about how we work from our Recipe here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers">https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous start-up equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch provided in the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team building events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited time off</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong><br />Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don't. It's a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it's a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Use AI at Tebi</strong><br />We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and improve but doesn't make the last call. If there's a smarter way to do something, we want to find it.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tebi/senior-product-manager-ai-team-amsterdam-124771","tags":["Product & Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794606018},{"slug":"defense-success-manager-france-amsterdam-379557","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Defense Success Manager, France","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Defense Success Manager, you own what happens to our most strategic defense and sovereign accounts after the build: you make deployed AI stick in real workflows — often in restricted or disconnected environments — keep production commitments healthy, defend renewals, and source the expansion signals that Sales closes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral's Solutions teams (Deployment Strategists and Forward Deployed Engineers) co-create high-value AI use cases with customers in these environments. Your job is to make those investments successful beyond delivery — adopting what has been built, operating it with confidence, demonstrating its impact, and scaling value across the institution. You will work with mission owners, program stakeholders, end users, security and IT teams, and across Mistral with Solutions, Product, Engineering and Support.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a high-volume, ticket-queue customer success role. Portfolios are small and deep — typically one or two flagship accounts plus a small number of adjacent programs. It calls for a strategic account mindset, the technical judgment to navigate complex and constrained deployment environments, and the energy to build the customer success function as Mistral grows. Travel to customer sites, including secure facilities, is a regular part of the job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will join on one of two tracks (and can move between them):</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adoption track</strong> — embedded in flagship programs while Solutions is still delivering. You own the adoption and change-management motion around the build: user waves, enablement, champions, training programs, and the evidence that proves value is landing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational track</strong> — you take accounts through a structured handover once Solutions completes delivery, and own the run phase end-to-end: operational health, value realization, renewals, and expansion signals.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In both tracks you operate in close partnership with Solutions: they deliver and hand over; you own post-handover; they re-engage on expansion signals. Occasionally, account teams will also pull you into late-stage pre-sales — authoring the customer training and scale-up plan that gives a buyer confidence in the rollout.</p><h2><br /><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><h3><br />Own the customer success and value plan</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a clear view of each account's objectives, stakeholders, deployed use cases, commitments and risks. Translate it into a shared success plan with owners, milestones and measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish a practical operating cadence with customer sponsors, business owners, IT and delivery teams. Lead success reviews that make progress, risks, decisions and next steps clear.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define a baseline and track the outcomes that matter for each use case: adoption and usage against entitled seats, customer satisfaction, operational health and business impact. Turn the evidence into a clear value narrative.</p></li></ul><h3>Make deployment realities part of the success plan</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand how each customer's deployment model — on-premises, VPC or serverless — affects the products and use cases they can access, operate and scale. Validate the specifics with the technical teams rather than assuming feature parity or identical operating models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify the practical implications of deployment choices: security and data requirements, access and integrations, release and upgrade cadence, available features, capacity, observability and support processes. Explain the trade-offs clearly to customer and Mistral stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate those constraints into an actionable adoption plan: align enablement and release communications with the version the customer actually runs, account for security approvals and upgrade windows, and agree how to measure usage when telemetry is limited.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot risks early, qualify their impact on adoption, renewal or value, and coordinate the right Solutions, Product, Engineering or Support owners to resolve them. Set clear expectations without making unvalidated technical or roadmap commitments.</p></li></ul><h3>Drive adoption, autonomy and sustained value</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help customer teams move from a delivered use case to regular, effective use. Identify the users, workflows and change-management needs that determine whether it sticks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate onboarding, training, product updates and hands-on enablement with the right Mistral and customer teams. Develop customer champions and train-the-trainer motions so adoption scales beyond direct Mistral involvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the transition from delivery to run: clarify operational ownership, support and escalation paths, and the resources users need to succeed independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor adoption and customer health, investigate where usage or value is falling short, and lead a coordinated plan to address the causes.</p></li></ul><h3>Defend and grow the commercial relationship</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the renewal motion for your accounts: know every renewal date, the auto vs non-auto renewal terms, and the risk story behind each one. Run the renewal play early — no surprises at renewal time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and improve account NRR. Identify new use cases, teams and expansion opportunities, and share them with the account team grounded in demonstrated value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead business reviews with the account team: value delivered, risks owned, decisions needed, roadmap asks.</p></li></ul><h3>Bring the customer voice into Mistral</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather and qualify feedback from users, technical teams and sponsors. Distinguish enablement needs from product gaps, deployment constraints and support issues, and route each to the right owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track important requests and communicate progress and limitations back to the customer, while Product and Engineering retain ownership of product and technical decisions.</p></li></ul><h3>Build the company as well as the account</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create the playbooks, success plans, handover practices and measurement approaches that are missing. Test them with customers, improve them, and make them reusable across accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring structure to ambiguity: identify what needs to happen, make a plan, mobilize the right people and follow through — without waiting for a perfect process or detailed instructions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Roughly a fifth of your time is protected, rotating build time for exactly this work; it is part of the job, not extra to it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience owning outcomes for enterprise or institutional customers of technical products or deployed solutions — adoption <strong>and</strong> commercial outcomes (retention, renewal, expansion), not relationship management or activity reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong technical fluency in secure enterprise deployment models.</strong> You can identify what a deployment type (on-premise, disconnected, air-gapped) means for available features, telemetry, upgrades and accreditation, and you validate specifics with technical teams instead of assuming parity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to engage credibly with architects, engineers, IT and security stakeholders, while translating technical trade-offs into clear implications for mission owners and executives. You know when to bring in a deeper technical expert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfort operating under security, compliance and confidentiality constraints</strong>, including restricted or classified environments and strict information-handling rules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership and builder energy. You have created structure or improved a process in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment and are motivated to build a company, not wait for clear directions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication, stakeholder management and execution skills. You align teams without formal authority, surface risks early and drive decisions through to completion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical and commercially minded: you can define meaningful success metrics with imperfect data, assess customer health, and are comfortable carrying renewal and NRR accountability.</p></li></ul><h3><br />Nice to have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience serving defense, public sector or critical infrastructure customers, including sovereign or classified programs.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI, machine learning, data platforms or complex enterprise software, including production deployments in regulated or security-sensitive environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working alongside deployment, engineering or professional services teams on custom use cases, and the transition from implementation to ongoing operation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with public procurement, framework agreements and multi-year option structures.</p></li></ul><h2>Security &amp; Compliance criteria</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Eligibility:</strong> must hold citizenship in the target territory (France for now).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clearable:</strong> must meet all local requirements for high-level security clearance (e.g. no criminal record, fulfillment of national service obligations).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mistralai/defense-success-manager-france-amsterdam-379557","tags":["Solutions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794606015},{"slug":"enterprise-success-manager-nl-emea-amsterdam-311122","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Enterprise Success Manager, NL (EMEA)","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Enterprise Success Manager at Mistral, you own what happens to our most strategic enterprise accounts <em>after</em> the build: you make deployed AI stick in real workflows, keep production ARR healthy, defend renewals, and source the expansion signals Sales closes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral's Solutions teams create high-value AI use cases with our customers. Your job is to make those investments successful beyond delivery — adopting what has been built, operating it with confidence, measuring its business impact, and scaling value across the organization. You will work with customer sponsors, business teams, IT and security stakeholders, and across Mistral with Solutions, Product, Engineering and Support.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a high-volume, ticket-queue customer success role. Portfolios are small and deep. It calls for a strategic account mindset, the technical judgment to navigate complex deployment environments, and the energy to build the customer success function as Mistral grows.<br /><br /><strong>You will join on one of two tracks (and can move between them):</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adoption track</strong> — embedded in flagship transformations <em>while</em> Solutions is still delivering. You own the adoption and change-management motion around the build: user waves, enablement, champions, training programs, and the measurement that proves value is landing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational track</strong> — you take accounts through a structured handover once Solutions completes delivery, and own the run phase end-to-end: operational health, value realization, renewals, and expansion signals.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In both tracks you operate in close partnership with Solutions: they deliver and hand over; you own post-handover; they re-engage on expansion signals. Occasionally, account teams will also pull you into late-stage pre-sales — authoring the customer training and scale-up plan that gives a buyer confidence in the rollout, a motion already credited in a major European win.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><h3><br />Own the customer success and value plan</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a clear view of each account's objectives, stakeholders, deployed use cases, commitments and risks. Translate it into a shared success plan with owners, milestones and measurable outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish a practical operating cadence with customer sponsors, business owners, IT and delivery teams. Lead success reviews that make progress, risks, decisions and next steps clear.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define a baseline and track the outcomes that matter for each use case: adoption and usage against entitled seats, customer satisfaction, operational health and business impact. Turn the evidence into a clear value narrative.</p></li></ul><h3>Make deployment realities part of the success plan</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand how each customer's deployment model — on-premises, VPC or serverless — affects the products and use cases they can access, operate and scale. Validate the specifics with the technical teams rather than assuming feature parity or identical operating models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify the practical implications of deployment choices: security and data requirements, access and integrations, release and upgrade cadence, available features, capacity, observability and support processes. Explain the trade-offs clearly to customer and Mistral stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate those constraints into an actionable adoption plan: align enablement and release communications with the version the customer actually runs, account for security approvals and upgrade windows, and agree how to measure usage when telemetry is limited.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot risks early, qualify their impact on adoption, renewal or value, and coordinate the right Solutions, Product, Engineering or Support owners to resolve them. Set clear expectations without making unvalidated technical or roadmap commitments.</p></li></ul><h3>Drive adoption, autonomy and sustained value</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help customer teams move from a delivered use case to regular, effective use. Identify the users, workflows and change-management needs that determine whether it sticks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate onboarding, training, product updates and hands-on enablement with the right Mistral and customer teams. Develop customer champions and train-the-trainer motions so adoption scales beyond direct Mistral involvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the transition from delivery to run: clarify operational ownership, support and escalation paths, and the resources users need to succeed independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor adoption and customer health, investigate where usage or value is falling short, and lead a coordinated plan to address the causes.</p></li></ul><h3>Defend and grow the commercial relationship</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the renewal motion for your accounts: know every renewal date, the auto vs non-auto renewal terms, and the risk story behind each one. Run the renewal play early — no surprises at renewal time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and improve account NRR. Identify new use cases, teams and expansion opportunities, and share them with the account team grounded in demonstrated value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead business reviews with the account team: value delivered, risks owned, decisions needed, roadmap asks.</p></li></ul><h3>Bring the customer voice into Mistral</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather and qualify feedback from users, technical teams and sponsors. Distinguish enablement needs from product gaps, deployment constraints and support issues, and route each to the right owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track important requests and communicate progress and limitations back to the customer, while Product and Engineering retain ownership of product and technical decisions.</p></li></ul><h3>Build the company as well as the account</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create the playbooks, success plans, handover practices and measurement approaches that are missing. Test them with customers, improve them, and make them reusable across accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring structure to ambiguity: identify what needs to happen, make a plan, mobilize the right people and follow through — without waiting for a perfect process or detailed instructions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Roughly a fifth of your time is protected, rotating build time for exactly this work; it is part of the job, not extra to it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5+ years of experience</strong> in customer-facing roles, such as Customer Success, Delivery/Implementation, or Solutions Consulting, ideally in a technical AI or SaaS environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning outcomes for enterprise customers of technical products or deployed solutions — adoption <strong>and</strong> commercial outcomes (retention, renewal, expansion), not relationship management or activity reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong technical fluency in enterprise deployment models.</strong> You can identify what a deployment type (on-premises, VPC, serverless) means for available features, telemetry, upgrades and security reviews, and you validate specifics with technical teams instead of assuming parity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to engage credibly with architects, engineers, IT and security teams, while translating technical trade-offs into clear business implications for executives and users. You know when to bring in a deeper technical expert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership and builder energy. You have created structure or improved a process in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment and are motivated to build a company, not wait for clear directions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication, stakeholder management and execution skills. You align teams without formal authority, surface risks early and drive decisions through to completion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical and commercially minded: you can define meaningful success metrics, assess customer health, and are comfortable carrying renewal and NRR accountability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; professional French strongly preferred (a significant share of our enterprise base is French-speaking).</p></li></ul><h3>Nice to have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI, machine learning, data platforms or complex enterprise software, including production deployments in regulated or security-sensitive environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working alongside deployment, engineering or professional services teams on custom use cases, and the transition from implementation to ongoing operation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building adoption, change-management or customer education programs across large organizations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at a forward-deployed, solutions-led company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mistralai/enterprise-success-manager-nl-emea-amsterdam-311122","tags":["Solutions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794606015},{"slug":"jr-ai-engineer-amsterdam-262980","company_name":"433","title":"Jr. AI Engineer","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><em>Are you passionate about football and technology? This is your chance! At 433, we are looking for a Junior AI Engineer to join our AI team.</em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>WE ARE 433<br></strong>With almost 80 million followers and over 5 billion impressions per month, 433 is the home of football on social media. We create and share the best football content across all platforms, worldwide. Our massive fanbase includes more than 15,000 professional football players, among them Cristiano Ronaldo, Kylian Mbappé, and Erling Haaland. From our headquarters in Amsterdam, we bring locker room humor and pure football passion to fans all around the world.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong> </p><p>We are looking for a motivated Junior AI Engineer to join our AI team. This role is ideal for someone who is passionate about Large Language Models, AI-powered automation and eager to gain hands-on experience with production-grade AI solutions.</p><p>Our team develops and maintains innovative AI solutions, including: </p><ul><li><p>AI-driven content automation, using LLM pipelines to generate, enrich, and curate content at scale;</p></li><li><p>Combining image processing techniques with visual AI models to generate high-quality graphics and visual assets;</p></li><li><p>Cloud-based pipelines, supporting scalable automation and data engineering;</p></li><li><p>Creating Python-based solutions for internal teams and products.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Assist in building and maintaining end-to-end LLM-based workflows, from code development to deployment and scheduling;</p></li><li><p>Work with multimodal AI models (text and image);</p></li><li><p>Experiment with image and video processing using Python;</p></li><li><p>Help with data preparation, testing, and evaluation of AI outputs;</p></li><li><p>Participate in product meetings and contribute ideas to ongoing AI projects. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>YOUR PLAYER PROFILE</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, AI, Data Science, or a related field (or equivalent experience); </p></li><li><p>You live in or around Amsterdam (already in The Netherlands); </p></li><li><p>Looking forward to work at our office for 4 days per week;</p></li><li><p>Proficiency in Python programming;</p></li><li><p>Basic understanding of Large Language Models and how they are used in applications;</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of SQL for database querying and data manipulation;</p></li><li><p><span style="color:#222222">Familiarity with AI-powered coding agents, such as Claude Code or OpenAI Codex;</span></p></li><li><p>Familiarity with APIs and structured data formats (JSON, REST);</p></li><li><p>Strong curiosity and willingness to learn modern AI tooling; </p></li><li><p>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;</p></li><li><p>Ability to work independently and as part of a team; </p></li><li><p>Good communication skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>NICE TO HAVE</strong></p><ul><li><p>Familiarity with Docker, Airflow, Git;</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with multimodal or visual AI models;</p></li><li><p>Basic knowledge of cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP);</p></li><li><p>Interest in RAG pipelines, AI agents, or MLOps concepts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>OUR OFFER</strong></p><ul><li><p>Hands-on experience with state-of-the-art AI technologies;</p></li><li><p>Mentorship from experienced AI and machine learning engineers;</p></li><li><p>Exposure to real-world, production AI systems;</p></li><li><p>A competitive salary, pension plan, and flexible vacation days;</p></li><li><p>A daily catered lunch and fresh fruit at our Amsterdam office;</p></li><li><p>Annual sports tournaments, team outings, and Friday afternoon drinks;</p></li><li><p>A dynamic and creative work environment with colleagues who share the same passion. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Do you want to contribute to the global growth of 433 and make an impact in the football world? Apply now!</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/433/jr-ai-engineer-amsterdam-262980","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam , Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1794605478},{"slug":"graduate-risk-analyst-amsterdam-171787","company_name":"Imc","title":"Graduate Risk Analyst","description":"&lt;p&gt;Your IMC journey begins with a three-week Global Trainee Program led by our seasoned engineers and traders, during which you’ll link up with graduates from all IMC regions: Europe, the United States, India and Asia-Pacific. During this traineeship, you’ll learn more about IMC, the basics of trading and options theory. Training continues back at your local office, where you’ll receive support from a dedicated mentor. As a Graduate Risk Analyst, you operate at the beating heart of our business: in the dealing room of IMC’s Amsterdam office. Your work supports IMC’s critical day-to-day risk management activities, including the monitoring and analysis of our markets, as well as our credit, liquidity, and operational risks. What happens next is up to you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR CORE RESPONSIBILTIES &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert in options, financial markets, and how IMC applies algorithmic trading as a market maker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the ongoing development of IMC’s proprietary risk management systems, together with our Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse developments in the markets in which we trade and identify risks and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an integral part of your team by advising on limit requests, monitoring intraday and overnight risks, and discussing key exposures with our trading desks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR SKILLS AND EXPERIENCES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent or upcoming graduates seeking to join IMC full-time in February 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An academic background in Mathematics, Physics and/or Econometrics or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in a programming language is preferred (Python, MATLAB or R)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-class analytical skills and a desire to solve complicated problems creatively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in financial markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: If you have already applied for this position during the current recruitment season and were not selected, you may reapply when the next recruitment season begins in Summer 2027. We encourage you to focus on enhancing your skillset before reapplying.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to current U.S. immigration and visa restrictions, some candidates may not be eligible to obtain the U.S. business visa required as part of our Global Traineeship Programme. As the programme includes mandatory training in the United States shortly after joining, we are unfortunately unable to proceed with applications from candidates who are unable to obtain the required visa within the programme timeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;If you are a dual passport holder of another nationality or a European citizen who wants to relocate back to Europe, you remain welcome to apply and should inform our campus recruitment team of your situation:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/imc/graduate-risk-analyst-amsterdam-171787","tags":["Risk Management"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1794596129},{"slug":"director-of-finance-ecosystem-amsterdam-85525","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Director of Finance - Ecosystem","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Strategic Finance, Planning &amp; Analysis team drives financial performance management across Prosus's global ecosystems - partnering with operating companies and Group Finance to ensure targets are met and capital is deployed effectively. The EU ecosystem team sits at the centre of Prosus's ambition to build a leading lifestyle e-commerce platform in Europe, and this Director role is the financial engine behind that ambition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the full Strategic FP&amp;A function for Prosus's European portfolio, managing the annual budgeting, planning, and forecasting cycle across a multi-entity, multi-country ecosystem, and leading the operating cadences that keep business unit CFOs, ecosystem leads, and Group Finance aligned. Within your first 60 days, you'll have established a working rhythm with every BU and minority investment finance team in the region. Within your first quarter, you'll hold full ownership of the EU ecosystem budgeting and forecasting cycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an active moment for the portfolio. M&amp;A and divestiture activity is ongoing, and you'll be a direct contributor to at least one strategic transaction within your first year,  not as a reviewer, but as a hands-on partner to the ecosystem leads driving those decisions. The team you'll lead is five to six direct reports; developing their capabilities and raising the bar on finance practice across the BU finance teams is as much a part of the role as the numbers themselves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn't a reporting function. This is financial leadership for one of Prosus's most strategically significant regions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in systems and act with precision. You're comfortable holding the full picture of a complex, multi-entity portfolio while also rolling up your sleeves on the analysis that makes a business case credible or a forecast defensible. Ambiguity doesn't slow you down - you move forward with the information available, surface the brutal facts clearly, and adjust as the picture sharpens.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built trust with senior stakeholders before - CFOs, business leads, Group Finance counterparts, not just by managing up but by being the person in the room who brings clarity. You give direct, evidence-based points of view and create space for the people around you to do the same. You care about the growth of your team as much as the quality of the output, and you understand that both are how a finance function earns its seat at the table.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Deep experience in finance or FP&amp;A at group or multi-entity level, with a background in digital economy, e-commerce, consumer internet, or a closely adjacent sector</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Proven ability to lead end-to-end budgeting, forecasting, and planning cycles across complex, matrixed organisations - coordinating multiple finance teams toward a single, coherent view</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Hands-on track record analysing financial statements, business cases, and performance data to surface actionable insight for senior decision-makers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Comfortable partnering directly with business unit CFOs and ecosystem leads on strategic projects including M&amp;A, divestiture, and performance benchmarking with the credibility to challenge and the judgement to know when to align</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Experience managing and developing a finance team, with a genuine investment in building capability at every level</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Fluent English communication, written and spoken, with the ability to translate financial complexity into clear, concise narratives for diverse audiences</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Familiarity with Group Finance functions (tax, treasury, reporting, consolidation) and how a finance function at this level interfaces with each</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Experience with Hyperion or OneStream is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Background in minority investment oversight or portfolio company finance is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Exposure to multi-country or cross-border finance environments in Europe is a plus</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Typical Day</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your day might begin with a performance review call with a business unit CFO - working through the latest actuals, flagging variances, and agreeing on the narrative before it reaches Group Finance. From there, you're likely in the detail: a forecast model that needs stress-testing, a business case for a potential acquisition, or a consolidation question that cuts across tax, treasury, and reporting.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Throughout the day, your team is moving in parallel - running analyses, preparing materials, coordinating with BU finance counterparts across the EU. You check in, unblock, and give direct feedback. By afternoon, you might be in a working session with an ecosystem lead on a live strategic project, or preparing the ecosystem performance summary that feeds into the Group FP&amp;A cycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Global Impact: Play a crucial role in shaping the future of global commerce.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Growth Opportunities: Expand your expertise through diverse global challenges and unique opportunities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Innovative Culture: Join a forward-thinking team that values strategic insights and fosters continuous innovation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Creative Environment: Engage in work that encourages creativity and constant improvement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">-